opitulemused_en:
- At the end of the course the student is able to:
- -	explain the nature of the main institutes of the international private law;
- -	understand the different parts of the international private law and their specific features in case of  application those principles;
- -	apply and use the norms of international private law by solving the cases (to present a written legal argumentation);
- -	use the legal literature and the case law by solving the cases;
- -	apply and use different methods of interpretation in order to explain the content and the aim of the norms of international private law.

- Student:
- understands and follows the work ethic and organization in the work environment;;
- can do teamwork and analyze his/her role in it;
- evaluate and analyze the development of his/her professional knowledge and skills in practice.
- The practice is related to the parts of career planning such as self-analysis (eg ability to analyze and interpret professional experience), knowledge of possibilities (eg have an idea of the professional identity of professions related to their specialty) and planning (eg ability to plan their working time).

- After completing the course the student knows
- 1) the epidemiology, etiology, pathogenesis and prophylaxis of more frequent surgical diseases in children;
- 2) the clinical picture and possible complications of surgical diseases in children;
- 3) contemporary clinical methods of patient investigation;
- 4) treatment methods, incl operative treatment, and indications for their usage, as well as time limits of operative treatment;
- The student is able to
- 1) take the anamnesis, carry out clinical examinations of a paediatric surgery patient and to analyse the results of paediatric clinical tests;
- 2) draw up a plan for examinations and analyse their results;
- 3) make clinical diagnosis, explain it on the basis of differential diagnosis;
- 4) determine indications for conservative or surgical treatment;

- A student who has passed the subject:
- * understands the operating mechanisms of the economy as a whole;
- * knows the logic of the structure of the micro- and macroeconomics` model of economy, the premises and the possible conclusions;
- * can analyse the standard situations dealt with in economic theory on the basis of a verbal, graphic and mathematical model;
- * can describe the problems which arise in economic practice as a theoretical model;
- * can critically assess the practical application possibilities of such a model;
- * has, on the basis of concrete models, become acquainted with the problems` abstract analysis possibilities and can use these skills in further studies and professional work.

- After the course, the student:
- 1. Knows how to classify and simplify the PDEs;
- 2. Is able to compile a PDE to describe some simple physical processes and phenomena;
- 3. Is capable of applying the separation of variables to solve PDEs;
- 4. Is capable of applying the method of Green's function to solve PDEs;
- 5. Is capable of applying the Fourier and Laplace integral transforms to solve PDEs;
- 6. Knows and is able to make use of the most important special functions.

- After passing the course student
- 1. is able to express his/her ideas in correct Estonian;
2. knows the rules how to write the mathematical text in general;
3. knows how to write mathematical text correctly in Estonian;

- The student will be able to
- - Define and explain basic concepts related to proof systems, logic programming and non-classical logics (modal logic, temporal logic, Hoare logic);
- - Derive formulas in a proof system with given axioms and rules;
- - Apply the resolution method to deduce conclusions from a set of premises;
- - Analyze the behavior of programs and systems using temporal logic;
- - Prove the correctness of simple programs using program logic.

- Upon completion of this course, the student is expected to:
1. Cognize physics as a science that investigates the most general causal relationships, generates the models of natural phenomena and broadens the internal and external limits of vision;
2. Express the basic principles of the physical concept of the nature (such as atomistic principle, energetic minimum, absolute speed, wave-particle dualism, uncertainty principle), and refer to their exertion;
3. Use the vocabulary introduced at the lectures during the scientific discussions, make difference between important and unimportant information, and apply physical terminology in a correct way;
4. Possess the knowledge considering the mathematical background and calculus necessary for the description of physical processes (e.g., graphical representations, differentiation and integration, application of complex numbers), and recognize the main attributes and occurrence conditions of main functions present in physics (e.g., linear, power, exponent, harmonic); 5. Know the basic definitions belonging to the current physical concept of the world within the limits of the vocabulary (30 pages of A4 format) available on the web page of the course;
6. Solve the physical problems within the limits of example exercises available via the web support of the course.

- After passing the course student
- Upon completion of the course students can:
- efficiently plan their writing process (schedule, goals etc.)
- use relevant sources of practical language management to ensure that the text is written in good style and complies with orthography rules;
- format various non-fiction texts electronically;
- analyse, based on feedback, their strengths and weaknesses as writers in order to make the writing process more efficient.

kirjeldus_et:
Käsitletakse digitaalse arhiveerimise ja elektroonilise dokumendihalduse mitmekülgsust ja keerukust. Tegeldakse järgmiste teemadega: 
*	teoreetilised ja tehnoloogilised alused; 
*	valdkonna põhiprintsiibid; 
*	rahvusvahelised standardid ja Eesti regulatsioonid; 
*	aktuaalsed tehnoloogilised lahendused.

kirjeldus_en:
During the course the complexity and versatility of digital archiving and electronic records management will be covered. Following topics will be discussed: 
*	theoretical and technological concepts; 
*	main principles of the domain;
*	international standards and Estonian regulations; 
*	actual solutions.

opitulemused_en:
- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- *	knows the theoretical and technological concepts of digital preservation;
- *	knows the main principles of electronic records management;
- *	has the overview of main international standards related to digital archiving and electronic records management;
- *	has overview of most common technological solutions in digital archiving and electronic records management.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: FLAJ.02.137 | Nimi (ET): Digitaalne arhiivindus ja dokumendihaldus | Nimi (EN): Digital Archives and Records Management | EAP: 3.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Aigi Rahi-Tamm, Tarvo Kärberg | Kirjeldus: Käsitletakse digitaalse arhiveerimise ja elektroonilise dokumendihalduse mitmekülgsust ja keerukust. Tegeldakse järgmiste teemadega: 
*	teoreetilised ja tehnoloogilised alused; 
*	valdkonna põhiprintsiibid; 
*	rahvusvahelised standardid ja Eesti regulatsioonid; 
*	aktuaalsed tehnoloogilised lahendused. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Testide rahuldav sooritamine. | Hindamise meetod: Positiivse tulemuse saamiseks peab testide aritmeetiline keskmine olema suurem või võrdne kui 51 % maksimumist.

opitulemused_en:
- The student who has completed the module:
- *	Has deepened and supplemented the knowledge of international law or human rights, acquired during the studies;
- *	Has applied acquired knowledge in different practical situations;
- *	Has developed practical skills to solve more complex legal problems and draft legal documents;
- *	Has improves team-work and communication skills;
- *	Has familiarised himself/herself with the culture, ethics and customs of professional organisations, and observes them during the practical training.
- **     Has developed an understanding of how to design and deliver a coherent teaching module, taking into account the learners' needs and developing accordingly learning objectives, teaching content and materials, appropriate methods, evaluation (only for for students who continue with Human Rights and Education)
- The student chooses one practice according to his/her preferences:
- 1.	International Law Practice (P2OG.02.215)
- 2.	Human Rights Law Practice (P2OG.02.216)
- The final result of practice is either passed or not passed.

- On successful completion of this course, students will be able to:
- * describe and argue the main issues related to fuzzy logic and soft computing;
- * use properly at least two of the soft computing techniques;
- * identify and implement a suitable soft computing technique to solve a given problem.

- A student, after taking the course:
- Knows the basics of information theory;
- Is familiar with the fundamentals of coding;
- Knows information channels and related theory;
- Is familiar with the basic of ergodic theory;
- Knows the maximal entropy principle;
- Is able to read information-theoretical literature;
- Is not the person (s)he used to be.

- Intended learning outcomes. The learner
- - has prepared the implementation of the business idea (incl analyzed the market, created business model, analyzed financial aspects, composed marketing plan, analyzed needed resources etc);
- - has developed a product or service mockup.

- After completion of the course the students will be able to:
- 1)	describe epidemiology, aetiology, pathogenesis, clinical symptoms of kidney diseases;
- 2)	demonstrate practical skills in acquiring a complete history and physical examination of patients with kidney diseases;
- 3)	use for differential diagnosis laboratory and radiology techniques as well as to interpretate the data;
- 4)	describe management of patients with different clinical syndromes: proteinuria, hematuria, nephritic syndrome, nephrotic syndrome, rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis, acute kidney injury and chronic renal failure;
- 5)	estimate renal function and  to manage patient in different stage of chronic kidney disease;
- 6)	do treatment decisions for chronic kidney disease patients and to send patients in time to nephrologists for the start of renal replacement therapy;
- 7)	know acute kidney injury signs and symptoms as well as treatment principles including necessity of renal replacement therapy.

- After completing the course, students will:
- analyse variation in Spanish in a geographical, historical and social context;
- identify and interpret the causes and consequences of linguistic variation in different communicative situations;
- determine the geographic origin and social register of given examples of Spanish, provided that they possess characteristics representative of the topics and geographic areas treated in class.
- works with digitally available data and resources: gather, select and paraphrase information in order to compile a comprehensive presentation that takes into account their audience (fellow students) and the appropriate linguistic register. Choose impactful audio or video examples to illustrate their presentation and prepare slides appropriate for academic contexts. Reference used sources correctly.

- Student who have passed the course:
- - knows the main features of the scientific approach, the process of academic research and the basic concepts of scientific ethics;
- - is able to independently find relevant scientific literature, can write an analytical literature review and is able to correctly refer to the sources used;
- - has knowledge of methods for collecting and analyzing quantitative and qualitative data;
- - has knowledge of presenting research results to the audience.

hindamise_meetod:
Final grade is composed of the following parts: 
1) participation in seminars, accompanied by small assignments; 
2) pre-defence of bachelor thesis. If a student graduates by final exam, the pre-defence is substituted by a consultation/rehearsal for bachelor exam.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: MJ00.00.024 | Nimi (ET): Bakalaureuseseminar | Nimi (EN): Bachelor's Seminar | EAP: 3.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Diana Eerma, Mariia Chebotareva | Toimumisajad: Teisipäev, Kolmapäev, Pühapäev | Kirjeldus: Bakalaureuseseminar üldistab ja süvendab üliõpilaste teadmisi teadusliku uurimistöö tegemiseks. | Hindamise meetod: Final grade is composed of the following parts: 
1) participation in seminars, accompanied by small assignments; 
2) pre-defence of bachelor thesis. If a student graduates by final exam, the pre-defence is substituted by a consultation/rehearsal for bachelor exam.

opitulemused_en:
- A person passing the course:
-knows the basic facts in the history of medicine;
-knows the basic trends in the history of natural sciences,
-knows the basic connections between the medical thought with social history;
-knows the basic facts in the history of the Medical Faculty, Univ. of Tartu

- Students:
- - aquire the skills for choosing appropriate literature on personality and group relations theories;
- - are able to conduct personality tests;
- - are able to distinguish between different  personality theories;
- - are able to apply their skills in practice

- After finishing the course, the student:
- - knows the basic concepts related to the theory of relational databases;
- - understands the principles of relational database design and understands design dilemmas;
- - designs a data model in a known field using an ER diagram and is able to convert it into a relational model;
- - can read schemes created by other developers;
- - describes databases in SQL language;
- - creates queries to databases using the logic of creating queries in SQL;
- - normalizes the theory of functional dependencies using database schemas, if necessary;
- - creates queries in both relational algebra and SQL;
- - compiles different views of a given database;
- - creates and modifies functions, procedures and triggers;
- - understands why and how to index data;
- - can create back-ups of databases, user groups, documentation;
- - understands the advantages and limitations of relational databases;
- - knows what data mining is and how it relates to databases.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Hindamisele pääseb üliõpilane juhul, kui iseseisvate tööde loetelus välja toodud tegevused on tehtud. Kõik väljatoodud tegevused on kohustuslikud:
* On leitud praktikakoht ja sõlmitud praktikaleping (esitada Moodlesse));
* Praktikaplaanis on formuleeritud praktika eesmärgid ja ülesanded;
* Ülesanded on teostatud ja eesmärgid saavutatud;
* Võetud praktikabaasi poolne hinnang;
* Esitatud eneseanalüüsi sisaldav praktikaaruanne;
* Osaletud lõpuseminaril (kas oma õppetoolis või praktika lõpuseminaris).

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: LOKT.00.023 | Nimi (ET): Praktika | Nimi (EN): Practical Speciality Training | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: sügis | Õppeastmed: magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: loodus- ja täppisteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Piret Pikma | Kirjeldus: Käesoleva õppeaine raames läbib tudeng vähemalt kuuajalisele täiskoormusele vastava praktika mõnes keemia, farmaatsia või muu sarnase kallakuga teaduslikus või tootmisettevõttes. Praktika lõpus esitab tudeng kirjaliku aruande saadud teadmisest koos ülevaatega praktika raames läbi viidud praktilistest töödest. Arvestuse saamiseks esitatakse aruanne oponeeritava suulise ettekandena. Praktika aruannete kaitsmine toimub vähemalt kord semestris Keemia Instituudi direktori poolt määratud komisjoni ees. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Hindamisele pääseb üliõpilane juhul, kui iseseisvate tööde loetelus välja toodud tegevused on tehtud. Kõik väljatoodud tegevused on kohustuslikud:
* On leitud praktikakoht ja sõlmitud praktikaleping (esitada Moodlesse));
* Praktikaplaanis on formuleeritud praktika eesmärgid ja ülesanded;
* Ülesanded on teostatud ja eesmärgid saavutatud;
* Võetud praktikabaasi poolne hinnang;
* Esitatud eneseanalüüsi sisaldav praktikaaruanne;
* Osaletud lõpuseminaril (kas oma õppetoolis või praktika lõpuseminaris). | Hindamise meetod: Lõplik tulemus kujuneb eneseanalüüsi sisaldava praktikaaruande ning seminari ettekande ja arutelu põhjal.

opitulemused_en:
- At the end of the course, the students should be able to:
- 1) know the formation of human normal microbiota and its composition:
- 2) describe the host-microbiota interactions;
- 3) understand the associations between the microbiota and different infectious and non-infectious diseases;
- 4) know the factors that influence the microbiota and state the suitable methods for microbiota modulation.

- During the practice:
- * learn to use Raspberry Pi and Arduino to control externela devices;
- * get (first) knowledge about Linux;
- * learn basics and practical use of client-server architecture;
- * learn to communicate to and control of different wireless (WiFi, Bluetooth, IR, RF, GSM) and wired (Ehernet) devices;
- * learn to use different sensors: webcam, motion detector, temperature, pressure, humidity, flow sensors etc.;
- * learn to create autonomous power supply for remote devices;
- * learn to create initial app for Andrid operating system to control remote devices;
- * solve a individual real-life problem.

- After passing the course student
- 1. have knowledge and skills about geography topics to teach science at the first and second school stage; 
2. is competent to use the best teaching methods and study aids to teach science (geography topics)  at the first and second school stage;
3. is competent to create practical learning materials for students to encourage their learning of science at the second school stage.

kirjeldus_en:
In theory of probability are considered random event and his classical probability;
random variable and  probability distribution.
In the part of mathematical statistics on bases of samples the estimations of characteristics of population (point and interval estimators) and testing of hypothesis are treated.

opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course student
- After passing the course student
Passing through the module, a participant
*	understands the concept of the random event and the ruls to calculate his probability;
*	acquires basic principles for probabilistic characterization of random variables; 
*	knows the most common probability distributions (binomial, geometric, Poisson, exponential, uniform and normal distribution) and is able to use them;
*	knows the main rules of estimating the population characteristics on bases of samples (point estimators, interval estimators, put and test hypothesis);
*	knows and understands the essence of studied methods and is able to apply them in solving practical problems;

- After passing this course the student
- - can use fundamental programming constructions: variables, expressions, assignments, conditionals, iterations, procedures, recursion, regular expression, simple input/output;
- - knows basic datatypes and -structures (numeric types, booleans, strings, lists) and can use corresponding standard operations;
- - can analyze and explain the behavior of simple programs, and modify and expand them;
- - can design algorithms for solving simple problems, and implement, test and debug the corresponding program.

- After passing the course student
- Upon completion of the course students 
* are able to use the least-squares method for the processing of measurement results and for the estimation of A-type uncertainties;
* are able to make use of analogue as well as digital electric measurement instruments (ammeters, voltmeters, ohmmeters), take readings and fix their accuracy, and estimate the B-type uncertainty;
* are able to solve easier electronical tasks using Arduino
* can perform several optical measurements based on interference, diffraction or  absorption of light, use appropriate detectors, and estimate uncertainties;
* can perform measurements in the field of environmental physics (air humidity, speed of air flow);
* are able to calibrate a measurement instrument and to prepare a basic calibration certificate;
* can calculate combined standard uncertainties and expanded uncertainties;

- A student who has passed the subject:
- - is able to set short- and long-term goals and knows how to achieve them;
- - can manage the team, himself, and development activities related to the business idea;
- - knows how to define and analyze problems, set strategic goals, and implement them;
- - can find and analyze important background information for his business model/business plan draft
- - knows the principles of intellectual property and can assess the need for intellectual property protection;
- - have tested their business idea or prototype on potential customers;
- -has developed his presentation skills and prepared a sales pitch.

hindamise_meetod:
Arvestuse hinde kujunemise alused:
- täiendatud ärimudel/äriplaan või tööplaan;
- äriidee edasiarenduse kaitsmine, sisenemine inkubaatorisse, tegevuse alustamine ettevõtjana või analüüs, miks antud äriidee ei rakendu.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: MJCV.00.005 | Nimi (ET): Ettevõtluse eelinkubatsioon | Nimi (EN): Entrepreneurial Pre-Incubation | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe, doktoriõpe, integreeritud bakalaureuse- ja magistriõpe, magistriõpe, rakenduskõrgharidusõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Aivar Pere, Märt Summatavet, Piia Vettik-Leemet | Toimumisajad: Kolmapäev, Reede | Kirjeldus: Õppija rakendab ärimudeli ja -plaani koostamise, toote- ja teenuse arenduse  ning  ettevõtte käivitamisega seotud põhiteadmisi ja praktilisi oskuseid. Meeskonnaga lepitakse kokku nende lühi- ja pikaajalised eesmärgid ning kaardistatakse vajalikud tegevused, mida hinnatakse kord kuus toimuva vestlusega (kokku neli vestlust). Aine lõpeb ideede tutvustamise ja edasise tegevuskava esitamisega komisjonile. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Arvestusele pääsemise tingimusteks on edasiarendatud ärimudel või äriplaan, tegevuse alustamine ettevõtjana või kirjalik analüüs, miks antud äriidee ei õnnestu või ei rakendata. Mentoriga peab olema kooskõlastatud eesmärkide aruanne, mis on täidetud 60% ulatuses. | Hindamise meetod: Arvestuse hinde kujunemise alused:
- täiendatud ärimudel/äriplaan või tööplaan;
- äriidee edasiarenduse kaitsmine, sisenemine inkubaatorisse, tegevuse alustamine ettevõtjana või analüüs, miks antud äriidee ei rakendu.

opitulemused_en:
- A student that completes the course:  
- will have an overview of the content and organisation of the various art collections at the University of Tartu Library (collections of painting, early graphic arts, bookplates and objects);
- will be familiar with the history of their development;
- will be up-to-date and know how to use the art collection database.

- After passing this course the student
- - knows and can use fundamental programming constructions: variables, expressions, assignments, conditionals, loops, subroutines, recursion, simple input/output;
- - knows basic datatypes and -structures (numeric types, booleans, strings, lists etc) and can use corresponding standard operations;
- - can analyze and explain in detail the behavior of simple programs, and modify, complement and develop them;
- - can design algorithms for solving simple problems, and implement, test and debug the corresponding program.
- - can implement projects related to programming in collaboration with teammates.

hindamise_meetod:
Kursus tervikuna lõpeb eksamiga, milles on nii väliskaubandusteooria kui - poliitika kui ka monetaarse teooria küsimused (50 punkti). Lisaks eksamile annavad punkte ka
1) kontrolltöö väliskaubandusest (25 punkti); 
2) kodutöö (grupitöö)  välismajandusega seotud teemal  (22 punkti);
3) test praktikumis (3 punkti).

Seega kokku saab aines maksimaalselt 100 punkti. Hinded pannakse alljärgnevalt: A: kontrolltööde ja eksami punktide kogusumma vähemalt 90 punkti, B - vähemalt 80, C-70, D-60 ja E- vähemalt 50 punkti.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: MJRI.08.061 | Nimi (ET): Rahvusvaheline majandus | Nimi (EN): International Economics | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Priit Vahter, Urmas Varblane | Kirjeldus: Väliskaubanduse üldteooria osas esitatakse erinevad mudelid, millega on põhjendatud riikide vahelist kaubandust. Algul käsitletakse klassikalisi kaubandusteooriaid, seejärel järgneb ülevaade uusklassikalistest teooriatest (Heckscher-Ohlini teooria). Seejärel pööratakse suurt tähelepanu kaasaegsetele väliskaubandusteooriatele.  Välismajanduse monetaarne teooria annab ülevaate maksebilansi olemusest ja koostisosadest ning selle seostest vahetuskursi, hindade ja sissetulekute taseme ning kapitali liikumisega. Lisaks sellele selgitatakse raha- ja maksupoliitika mõju majanduse tasakaalule ning tutvustatakse rahvusvaheliste finantsorganisatsioonida tegevust. | Eeldusained: (SVMJ.05.006 "Mikroökonoomika") | Hindamise meetod: Kursus tervikuna lõpeb eksamiga, milles on nii väliskaubandusteooria kui - poliitika kui ka monetaarse teooria küsimused (50 punkti). Lisaks eksamile annavad punkte ka
1) kontrolltöö väliskaubandusest (25 punkti); 
2) kodutöö (grupitöö)  välismajandusega seotud teemal  (22 punkti);
3) test praktikumis (3 punkti).

Seega kokku saab aines maksimaalselt 100 punkti. Hinded pannakse alljärgnevalt: A: kontrolltööde ja eksami punktide kogusumma vähemalt 90 punkti, B - vähemalt 80, C-70, D-60 ja E- vähemalt 50 punkti.

opitulemused_en:
- After the course, the students are expected:
- 1. Analyzes various natural phenomena based on the laws and principles of physics and using correct terminology;
- 2. Critically evaluates information about physics, distinguishing between scientific and pseudoscientific information;
- 3. Motivate students to notice and explain natural phenomena and processes occurring in the surrounding environment using scientific methods;
- 4. Plans and supervises students' home projects.;

- After passing this course every student:
- 1. has an overview of the level of mathematical knowledge in Mesopotamia, Egypt, China, India, Japan and Islamic Countries;
- 2. knows main mathematicians and their schools in Ancient Greece;
- 3. knows the level of mathematical sciences in Europe during the period from Middle Ages until 17th century;
- 4. has an overview of the development of different fields of mathematics during the period from 18th to 20th century.

- Students who have taken the course are expected
- * to be able to use most essential optical measuring instruments;
- * to be skilled in executing the report of measurements.

- Upon completion of the course, the students will:
- 1) be aware of the ethical problems arising in teaching, able to discuss them systematically and thoughtfully and hence move towards the solutions;
- 2) be familiar with teachers' code of ethics and the society's expectations and demands for teachers, able to take a stand on these issues;
- 3) be aware of their own moral beliefs and values, of the sources of these, and able to evaluate them critically;
- 4) understand teacher's role as a values educator and the need to attend to the development of school's common values;
- 5) be familiar with the main methods of values education and have an understanding of using them while working with children.

- The attested student:
- is able to characterize the most important Renaissance and Baroque buildings and artworks, and can list the most important master artisans;
- is able to list and explain the sources and methods of study
- is able to explain the processes of commissioning and making of art
- is able to analyze the connections between art, power, religion etc.;
- is able to correctly use the art historical terminology
- is able to set the Estonian buildings and artworks in a wider historical and cultural context;
- is able to do teamwork.

- The students will be able to:
- 1) have theoretical knowledge - prevalence, etiology, diagnosis, treatment - of gastrointestinal and hepatobiliary diseases;
- 2) carry out a complete history and physical examination emphasizing the gastrointestinal system;
- 3) outline a diagnostic impression and a short differential diagnosis of gastrointestinal and hepatobiliary diseases;
- 4) suggest treatment and management of gastrointestinal and hepatobiliary diseases.

- - can listen actively, interview, be assertive, and manage conflict and negotiation situations;
- - can analyse his/her communication skills and manage self-training;
- - knows the good practice of communication;
- - perceives and can give different types of feedback; can be a motivating conversation partner;
- - has an overview of different work-related communication situations and knows how to implement different communicative competences according to need;
- - can notice and shape communication skills of children and the habit of following good practices of communication;
- - knows how to consider the communicative needs of different target groups;
- - is motivated to critically analyse and practice his/her own communicative competences constantly.

hindamise_meetod:
Eksamihinde kujunemine:
Suuline eksam, mis koosneb kahest osast: esimese osa moodustavad teoreetilised küsimuses, mis valmistatakse ette kirjalikul koos kohtupraktika kasutamise võimalusega;
teise osa moodustab kaasuse lahendamine (võimalusega kasutada õigusakte ja kohtupraktikat).

Lõplik tulmus kujuneb kirjaliku eksami alusel.
E - õigesti tehtud 51-60% eksamiülesandeid;
D - õigesti tehtud 61-70% eksamiülesandeid;
C - õigesti tehtud 71-80% eksamiülesandeid;
B - õigesti tehtud 81-90% eksamiülesandeid;
A -  õigesti tehtud 91-100% eksamiülesandeid.

