opitulemused_en:
- The student
acquires an overview of central themes of world literature and Estonian literature and acquires and understanding of the literary, cultural and generic specificities of their development;
is capable of applying acquired knowledge to the analysis of literary works from different periods and cultural regions and to draw parallels with other cultural phenomena.

- Upon completing the course, the student will be able to:
- 1.	Explain the mechanisms of the formation of chemical elements and their distribution in the universe and different spheres of the Earth;
- 2.	Apply the fundamental principles of thermodynamics and chemical kinetics in the context of geology;
- 3.	Understand the main geochemical classifications of chemical elements;
- 4.	Describe key geological processes using the distribution of chemical elements and their isotopes;
- 5.	Date rocks based on their radiogenic isotope composition;
- 6.	Understand the major geochemical cycles of the Earth;
- 7.	Understand the main applications and fields of geochemistry;
- 8.	Apply the aforementioned knowledge and skills to solve geochemical problems.

- After passing the course student
- A student who has passed the subject:
- understands the assumptions and logic behind the economic thinking (formal economic models)
- can describe many everyday problems as theoretical microeconomic models; 
- can analyze standard situations using microeconomic reasoning;
- can apply either verbal, graphic or mathematical models;
- has experience using formal models for analyzing real life problems;
- can critically assess the practical application possibilities of such a model;

