opitulemused_en:
- Student who passes the course:
- knows the principles, challenges and coordination that structure the work of a public sector organization;
- has attained work experience in a public sector organization;
- has applied at workplace knowledge, skills and values attained during academic studies;
- has learned to recognize and to develop social skills needed when working in an organization;
- has developed skills which prepare the student for work in public sector organization;
- has developed the skill of reflection on the practical application of attained academic knowledge and on the development on skills needed at future work place.

- A student who has successfully passed this course:
- a) knows the main concepts of strategic management;
- b) understands the theoretical and practical questions of strategic management, from the co-operational, employee and manager perspectives;
- c) is able to analyze and evaluate the organization and its environment from strategic perspective;
- d) is able to apply main methods/tools of strategic analysis
- e) has acquired skills and experiences for the analysis of holistic functioning of an organization;

- Upon completion of the course students can:
- - plan their writing process (setting goals; time management);
- - evaluate whether texts written by themselves or others meet the requirements of academic convention, including requirements for summarizing and referencing;
- - write well-structured texts with good style using relevant sources of practical language management;
- - give and receive feedback and make changes in their writing process based on it;
- - apply methods that support presentation when giving academic presentations;
- - format their texts according to the guidelines of their specialty or conventions of their field.

- A student who completed an internship:
- - knows different possibilities for working in his chosen profession;
- - you characterize the activities and main work processes of different companies;
- - analyzes the competencies important for working in the chosen profession;
- - reflects his experience and competencies in relation to the chosen profession and the companies he has met.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Eksamile pääsemise eelduseks on:
a) aktiivne praktikumides osalemine;
b) iseseisvate tööde õigeaegne sooritamine;(tööde loetelu ja tähtajad esitatakse kursuse käigus Moodle's);
b) kolme kontrolltöö positiivne sooritus.(Kontrolltööde järeletegemisvõimalus puudub; iga järgmine töö sisaldab 25% ulatuses eelnenud KT materjali).

opitulemused_en:
- After this course students will have basic knowledge on the following topics:
- base resources of computer systems - storage, computing power, bandwidth, software, resource virtualization; best practices in system administration; processes in system administration - planning, risk management, implementation, testing, maintenance, monitoring, documenting, service support, problem management;
- Acquired skills include:
- planning systems and services; implementing services; service monitoring; service maintenance; problem management in computer systems;

- Students
- - are able to describe culture through it's distinctive features and compare different definitions of culture;
- - are able to distinguish the main disciplines that analyze culture and their primary concepts;
- - understand the methodological principles of the theory of culture and are able to orientate in qualitative research methods;
- - are able to delineate cultural research object.

kirjeldus_et:
Kursusel osalemiseks ei nõuta eelteadmisi prantsuse keeles.
Semestris käsitletavad suhtlussituatsioonid ja sõnavara:
- enese ja teiste esitlemine (nimi, rahvus, elukutse);
- inimeste ja asjade tuvastamine või tutvustamine (Kes see on? Mis see on?);
- viisakusväljendid (tervitamisviisid, vabandamine jne);
- enesetutvustus, isikuandmed (nimi, vanus, elukoht, amet, perekonnaseis jne);
- töö ja õpingud;
- vaba aja tegevused, sport, maitse-eelistused;
- kodulinn ja elukoht;
- kuupäev, kellaaeg, ajakava;
- ettepaneku tegemine, nõustumine, keeldumine;
- Euroopa Liidu ja maailma riigid.
Grammatika:
- sissejuhatus grammatika terminoloogiasse;
- häälduse alused;
- numbrid;
- tegusõna pööramine olevikus;
- määrav, umbmäärane ja liitunud artikkel;
- nimisõna grammatiline sugu, omadussõna mees- ja naissoo vormid, mitmuse moodustamine;
- eessõna "de" kasutamine nimisõna ees (nimisõnalise täiendi sidumiseks või kuuluvuse väljendamiseks);
- eessõna kasutamine maa- ja kohanimede ees;
- eituslause;
- küsilause, küsisõnad;
- possessiivid ehk omastavad omadussõnad;
- isikulised asesõnad (lause alus, rõhuline asesõna);
- lähitulevik;
- "si" kasutamine (jah-vastus eitavas vormis esitatud küsimusele).

kirjeldus_en:
The course presupposes no preliminary knowledge of French.
The contents of  the course as communication situations and vocabulary related:
- presenting oneself and others (name, nationality, profession);
- identifying or introducing persons and objects (Who is this? What is this?);
- expressions of courtesy (greetings, apologies, etc.);
- introducing oneself, personal data (name, age, address, profession, marital status, etc.);
- work and studies;
- leisure activities, sports, preferences;
- hometown, living quarters;
- dates, time, schedule;
- making, accepting or refusing a proposition;
- EU and other countries.
Grammar topics:
- introduction to the grammar terminology;
- pronunciation rules;
- numbers;
- verb conjugation (present tense, indicative mood);
- article (definite, indefinite, contracted);
- nouns and adjectives (gender and number);
- prepositions "de" and "à";
- prepositions before countries' names and other place names;
- negative sentence;
- interrogative sentence, interrogative words;
- possessive adjectives;
- personal pronouns (subject pronouns and stressed pronouns);
- immediate future (futur proche);
- affirmative answer "si" to the negative question.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: HVLC.03.006 | Nimi (ET): Prantsuse keele algkursus I (inglise keele baasil), tase 0 > A1.1 | Nimi (EN): French for Beginners I (on the Basis of English), Level 0 > A1.1 | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe, doktoriõpe, magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Reet Alas | Toimumisajad: Esmaspäev, Kolmapäev | Kirjeldus: Kursusel osalemiseks ei nõuta eelteadmisi prantsuse keeles.
Semestris käsitletavad suhtlussituatsioonid ja sõnavara:
