opitulemused_en:
- The student:
- 1) can take part effortlessly in any conversation or discussion and can use language flexibly and effectively for social and professional purposes;
- 2) can formulate ideas and opinions with precision and to develop a subject in conversation;
- 3) can present clear, smoothly-flowing descriptions of complex subjects, developing particular points and rounding off with an appropriate conclusion;
- 4) can express himself in a clear, well-structured text, expressing points of view about complex subjects;
- 5) can write in an appropriate style complex letters, reports or essays which present a case with an effective logical structure.

- On successful completion of the course, the students will
- 1. know and use the basic terminology of foreign language teaching and assessment;
- 2. know the aims of foreign language (including Estonian as a second language) teaching in Estonian basic and secondary education and be able to specify foreign language learning objectives,
- 3. know the principles of foreign language course and lesson design and be able to apply them in the course and lesson design process;
- 4. be able to select activities and materials to meet the objectives of language teaching and learning;
- 5. know the principles of language assessment and be able to use them in the course design process and in the analysis of foreign language tests;
- 6. plan and execute the project in co-operation with their groupmates;
- 7. analyse critically the courses designed by themselves and their colleagues.

