opitulemused_en:
- A student
- - recognises grammar structures in written text in English and is able to find an adequate expression in Estonian;
- - can use modals, conditional sentences, adjectives in various contexts, adverbs, reported speech and simple passive voice;
- - knows the structure of sentences and can use the correct word order in different speeches;
- - uses acquired knowledge in oral as well as in written communication.

- After the course student:
- -	has a review of ethiology and physiology;
- -	is familiar with examination methods of visual acuity and knows principles of the optical correction;
- -	has an overview of the capabilities of different methods of the optical correction;
- -	is familiar with different types of the spectacles and contact lenses;
- -	has an overview about refractive surgery.

- Upon successful completion of the course the student:
- - is familiar with the objectives and structure of the Estonian Native Crafts study program;
- - knows the structure and house rules of the academy and the Estonian Native Crafts study program;
- - knows how to use the school information systems necessary for everyday studies;
- - is familiar with the main craft unions, their goals, and work order;
- - knows about opportunities to study and practice abroad;
- - aims at his / her professional studies and career choices.

- Student having participated in this subject:
- 1)	Has knowledge of theoretical bases of administrative court procedure;
- 2)	Knows the principles of administrative court procedure;
- 3)	Is able to determine the jurisdiction of the administrative court;
- 4)	Is skilled to file an action with an administrative court in conformity with formal and material requirements of a claim;
- 5)	Is ready to represent the parties and third persons in administrative court proceedings;
- 6)	Is prepared to take an advantage of the legal literature and case law for solving the case studies;
- 7)	Is able to analyse and solve the cases on administrative court procedure according to the respective methodology.

- After passing the course student
- - is motivated to use computers and to develop necessary programs for further studies;
- - can demonstrate basic programming constructs (branching, loops, subprogram) as programming sections;
- - can develop algorithms for simple text-based problems.

- Upon successful completion of the course students:
-	have received an overview of the development trends in Estonian folk costumes, of the influences and of the differences and similarities of the costumes as well as accessories of different regions, of the materials, design and ornamentation;
-	know and can distinguish different development periods of folk costumes;
-	know the influences of urbanization on folk costumes at the end of the 19th century;
-	have an overview of the influences of neighboring countries on Estonian folk costumes;
-	can use written resources on the basis of which are able to prepare, both in theory and in practice, folk costumes of different Estonian parishes for women, men and children.

- Successful student:
- - knows terminology of the project work and structure of projects;
- - can analyse the problem, set objectives, plan activities and resources;
- - can design simple project application.

- After passing this course the student:
- discusses problems recurring in history of culture and explains how political and social processes influence culture;
- explains the connections between the cultural and societal developments in Estonia and the rest of the world (Europe);
- poses research questions, compares and interprets historical primary sources and forms arguments based on relevant literature.

