opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course the student
1) knows the main terms from the speciality-relevant terminology;
- 2) can describe and analyze the main field-relevant issues in English;
- 3) can discuss the field-relevant issues both in Estonian and European context;
- 4) can make a presentation on a speciality-relevant topic.

- This lecture course teaches you to understand:
- mathematical presentation of oscillation and waves;
- impact of oscillations to constructions (buildings, bridges), to vehicles (ships, airplanes) to human organism, and to plants;
-  contribution of atmospheric column gases to greenhouse effect;
-  biological impact of UV-radiation;
-  dynamics of atmospheric ozone layer, ozone's defending and damaging role;
-  acoustics, ultrasound and infrasound.

The lecture course gives you a competence for:
- explain impact of mechanical oscillations to human organism and buildings;
-  evaluation of safe duration for working in vibrational environment;
-  calculation of total intensity of different sources of noise;
-  distinguishing, by a molecular formula, greenhouse and non-greenhouse gases;
-  planning duration of a sunbath, 
and many other interesting and useful skills.

- After passing the course student
- The student:
1) can use correctly French vocabulary and grammatical forms as well as French academic expressions;
2) is able to express points of view on complex subjects in a clear and well-structured text;
3) can write clear, smoothly-flowing texts in an appropriate style for a bachelor’s thesis and present an issue with logical structure.

- The student who graduate the course:
- - knows more about the biochemical composition of drinks;
- - is able to analyse the possible health issues of drinks on the consumer´s health.

- The student who has passed the course
- - is aware of the main groups of psychoactive drugs and knows the most important representative drugs;
- - knows their main effects and adverse effects, and understands their mechanisms of action;
- - is able to associate the principles of CNS physiology with the actions of psychoactive drugs;
- - is prepared to obtain novel information on psychoactive drugs.

- After completing the course the student should be able to:
- - read and understand simple texts in Russian;
- - use the vocabulary and grammar covered during the course in everyday situations;
- - get into social contact (to greet, to say goodbye, to introduce oneself, to thank, to apologies etc.);
- - talk about family, home town, hobbies, day schedule;
- - understand the basic structures of Russian grammar;
- - ask simple questions and answer them.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Presentation is done successfully if the following conditions are met:
a) presented at a pace that everyone can hear and follow, without much uncertainty, the student can use the support text created by himself, but not read it;
b) language errors must not hinder the understanding of the presentation, new or difficult words should be explained/translated (for example on a separate page/board);
c) suitable length (fits into the time frame 7-10 min);
d) the presentation has a clear structure;
e) proper presentation - a sufficient number of slides that meet the requirements of a good presentation.
Home reading. Answering individually (at the end of the semester).

