opitulemused_en:
- At the end of the course the student:
- 1. is able to use general legal vocabulary;
- 2. is familiar with the terminology of the areas of law covered in the course;
- 3. knows and is able to use electronic dictionaries;
- 4. is able to refer legal texts of various contents, especially in written form.

kirjeldus_et:
Üliõpilane viib kursust koordineeriva õppejõu juhendamisel läbi iseseisva praktika rakendades varem omandatud teadmisi rakenduslikust kultuurianalüüsist.  
Praktika raames üliõpilane:
- koostab koostöös ülikoolivälise partneriga uurimisprojekti plaani ja sõnastab praktika eesmärgid; 
- viib ülikoolivälise partneri juures läbi rakendusliku projekti;
- esitab kirjaliku praktikaaruande, milles analüüsib ja hindab kriitiliselt oma välitööde materjali, omandatud kogemust ja projekti raames ilmnenud eetilisi aspekte (s.h. kasutatud meetodeid ja nende rakendamist ja saadud tulemusi jm);
- esitab oma uurimuse tulemused ülikoolivälisele partnerile (kelle juures välitööd läbi viidi) sobivas vormis ja viisil.

kirjeldus_en:
Under the supervision the student is conducting an independent  practical project using knowledge related to applied cultural analysis.
The student:
-	is composing a research plan and aims of the study in collaboration with an external partner;
-	is conducting a practical project at an external partner;
-	presents a written work in which the collected materials, acquired experience and ethical issues are  critically analysed (e.g. methods and their application, the results etc.).
-	presents the final results of the study in a suitable media and form for the external partner.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: FLKU.03.091 | Nimi (ET): Rakendusantropoloogia praktika | Nimi (EN): The Practice of Applied Anthropology | EAP: 3.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe, magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Ester Bardone | Kirjeldus: Üliõpilane viib kursust koordineeriva õppejõu juhendamisel läbi iseseisva praktika rakendades varem omandatud teadmisi rakenduslikust kultuurianalüüsist.  
Praktika raames üliõpilane:
- koostab koostöös ülikoolivälise partneriga uurimisprojekti plaani ja sõnastab praktika eesmärgid; 
- viib ülikoolivälise partneri juures läbi rakendusliku projekti;
- esitab kirjaliku praktikaaruande, milles analüüsib ja hindab kriitiliselt oma välitööde materjali, omandatud kogemust ja projekti raames ilmnenud eetilisi aspekte (s.h. kasutatud meetodeid ja nende rakendamist ja saadud tulemusi jm);
- esitab oma uurimuse tulemused ülikoolivälisele partnerile (kelle juures välitööd läbi viidi) sobivas vormis ja viisil. | Eeldusained: (FLKU.03.035 "Etnograafiliste välitööde metodoloogia") VÕI (HVKU.03.002 "Etnograafiliste välitööde metodoloogia"); (HVKU.03.004 "Sissejuhatus rakendusantropoloogiasse") | Hindamise eeltingimused: Tööplaanis ette nähtud tegevused sooritatud, aruanne esitatud. | Hindamise meetod: Aruande ja praktikabaasi poolse juhendaja hinnangu põhjal.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course, the student:
- - understands texts on familiar and interesting topics, e.g. work, school, free time etc;
- - holds a fluent conversation on familiar and interesting topics;
- - gives a prepared presentation on a familiar topic, expressing themselves in simple, relatively clear and understandable language;
- - composes simple texts on familiar or interesting topics;
- - has acquired basic theoretical knowledge in the field of Norwegian philology;
- - understands differences between Estonian and Norwegian cultures, and takes them into account in both written and spoken communication.

- After completing the course, the student
- - has an overview of the phonological system of Swedish;
- - names the principles of forming speech sounds in Swedish and applies the acquired theoretical knowledge in practice;
- - knows the speech prosody characteristic to Swedish;
- - analyses simple phonetic material, applying the main principles of phonetic transcription;
- - is aware of the most common intonation and articulation problems in acquiring Swedish, and can notice and correct those problems in their own speech if needed.

- Upon completion of the course, participants:
1.	know how to use main databases of world languages /Ethnologue, WALS);
2.	know what is meant by the different bases of categorizing langauges and alo critics;  
3.	and how these categories is used depending on different aims of a research;
4.	know how to write Wikipedia entry and how to use sources for that.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) can describe and analyse projects;
- 2) can evaluate and, if necessary, recommend various project management methods;
- 3) can analyse aspects of financial activities and personnel in projects;
- 4) can analyse the influence of project management on an organisation in cooperation with specialists.

- After the course the student
- - Knows the effect of different types of data collection methods to the random nature of the frequency table and the basic distributional models for the frequency table, for its rows and columns;
- - Knows the dependence measures defined on the joint distribution of 2 categorical variables (relative risk, odds ratio, etc.), can interpret and estimate them;
- - Can test goodness-of-fit of data with the assumed distributional model, can test independence of categorical variables;
- - Knows the large sample as well the small sample tests;
- - Can model the categorical variable (binary, in special case) by other variables;
- - Can apply his/her knowledge on real data.

- Students having participated in this subject:
- -	Have profound knowledge on the material and procedural conditions of the claims based on the tort liability of public authorities;
- -	Are familiar with the conditions of the liability of member states under the EU law and with the relevant case law of the European Court of Justice;
- -	Are prepared to analyse the main theoretical legal standpoints and case law in this field and are ready to take posititions and make convincing arguments;
- -	Recognise the legal problems of the tort liability of public authorities in practice and are skilled to deliver a detailed case study.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: OIAO.05.038 | Nimi (ET): Riigivastutus | Nimi (EN): State Liability | EAP: 3.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Andra Laurand, Janar Jäätma, Kadri Palm, Tanel Saar | Kirjeldus: Kursuse raames käsitletakse õiguskaitsevahendeid, mille eesmärgiks on kaitsta ja taastada avalik-õiguslikus suhtes rikutud õigusi ning tagada isikule avaliku võimu poolt tekitatud kahju heastamine. Siia kuuluvad nii kahju ärahoidmisele ja vähendamisele suunatud esmased õiguskaitsevahendid kui ka kahju hüvitamise ja õigusvastaste tagajärgede kõrvaldamise nõuded. Lisaks käsitletakse EL-i õigusest tulenevat liikmesriigi vastutust. Kursuse põhirõhk on kaasusõppel. | Eeldusained: (OIAO.05.039 "Haldusõigus") VÕI (OIAO.05.002 "Haldusõigus") VÕI (P2OG.02.154 "Haldusõigus"); (P2OG.02.058 "Riigiõigus") VÕI (OIAO.05.040 "Riigiõigus") | Hindamise eeltingimused: 1) grupitööna kaasuste lahendamine ja ettekannete pidamine seminaris;
2) aktiivne osavõtt seminaridest. Kui üliõpilane pole seminariks ette valmistunud või ei osale grupitöös, jääb seminarist osavõtt arvestamata. | Hindamise meetod: Ainekursuse hinne kujuneb kirjaliku eksami hindest. Eksamile pääsemise eelduseks on seminarides osalemine ning kaasust lahendamine ja oponeerimine.  Eksam koosneb kahest teoreetilisest küsimusest (osatähtsus 10%+10%) ja ühest kaasusest (osatähtsus 80%). Positiivse hinde (vähemalt E) saamiseks peab punktisumma nii teooriaküsimuste eest moodustama vähemalt üle 50% kui ka kaasuse eest moodustama vähemalt üle 50 %.
Eksam kestab 90 minutit. Eksami sooritamisel on lubatud kasutada seadusi ja kaasuste lahendamise skeeme, vajadusel viitab õppejõud täiendavatele materjalidele.

opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course student
- A student that completes the course: 
- will be familiar with the history of art in the Renaissance period; 
- will be familiar with the works of outstanding artists and architects of the era; 
- will be able to speak and write about the art of the Renaissance.

- After successful completion of the course, student:
- 1. is able to utilise A/D converter and select suitable level of quantisation and sampling frequency;
- 2. knows how to sample and quantises a continuous signal and describes possible distortions and noise;
- 3. calculates convolution of two discrete signals and knows some applications;
- 4. has implemented DFT and understands the background of the operation, and is familiar with FFT;
- 5. has used and knows what are IIR and FIR filters;
- 6. has used various tools for signal processing;
- 7. has applied the covered DSP tools to solve a complex tasks;
- 8. has used various lab equipment for data acquisition and processing;
- 9. has learned to used the aforementioned tools in the language of Python.

- After successful completion, the student
- - is able refine robotics or prototyping project goals, estimate the expected outcomes, and put together a generalized plan and budget;
- - can divide a project in to tasks and milestones, determine the order of task, describe task dependencies/relations, estimate work hours, and assess results;
- - can provide project documentation in a written form and communicate technical information both in writing and orally;
- - has experience of working as a member of a larger team;
- - is able to anticipate potential problems and provide timely solutions;
- - can execute a technical robotics and/or prototyping project according the the project plan but adapt if the project requirements change.

- Students who have passed the programme successfully:
- 1.	know general peculiarities of manifestation of illnesses and treatment in older people (clinical examination, assessment before scheduled surgery, application of clinical guidelines in frail older people, potentially inappropriate medicines for older people);
- 2.	are able to perform basic comprehensive geriatric assessment (interRAI CA as an example) and use data of complete geriatric comprehensive assessment for planning of following diagnostics, treatment and care;
- 3.	know manifestations of essential geriatric syndromes/ problems and are capable of considering them in clinical practise (frailty in old age, dementia, delirium, malnutrition, falls, pain, urinary incontinence);
- 4.	are aware of general principles of long term health and social care arrangement and roles of different specialists; understand the role of a physician in an interdisciplinary care team;
- 5.	know and utilise principles of geriatric ethics (ageism, elderly abuse, advance directives).

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Uurimistöö kaitsmise eelduseks on juhendaja nõusolek töö kaitsmisele lubamiseks.

Uurimistöö esitamine ja kaitsmine vastavalt akadeemilisele kalendrile.
Uurimis- ja magistritööde juhendamise kord, kättesaadav kodulehel https://oigus.ut.ee/sites/default/files/inline-files/loputoo_nouded_kaitsmiskomisjoni_moodustamise_kord_ja_kaitsmise_kord.pdf

III. Üliõpilase õigused ja kohustused
3.1. Üliõpilasel on õigus saada juhendajalt kokkulepitud aegadel töö kohta tagasisidet. Tagasiside mittesaamisel võib üliõpilane pöörduda instituudi juhataja või tema asetäitja poole.
3.2. Üliõpilane on kohustatud:
3.2.1. võtma juhendajaga omavahelise koostöö ning juhendamise ajakava kokkuleppimiseks ühendust hiljemalt ühe kuu jooksul alates töö teema valimise tähtpäevast;
3.2.2. osalema juhendaja korraldatud kokkusaamistel;
3.2.3. pidama kinni kokkulepitud töö koostamise tähtpäevadest. Kokkuleppe puudumisel tuleb magistritöö terviktekst esitada juhendajale vähemalt kaks kuud ning uurimistöö terviktekst vähemalt üks kuu enne töö esitamise tähtpäeva;
3.2.4. võtma töö kirjutamisel arvesse juhendaja instruktsioone;
3.2.5. vastama juhendaja kirjale või informeerima tagasiside saatmise ajast viie tööpäeva jooksul või hiljem, kui selleks on mõjuv põhjus;
3.2.6. esitama juhendajale tagasiside andmiseks keeleliselt korrektselt vormistatud teksti.

hindamise_meetod:
Kaitsmine on hindeline (A-E).
Hinde kujunemisel arvestatakse:
- töö vastavust esitatud nõuetele (https://oigus.ut.ee/sites/default/files/inline-files/oigusteaduskonna_uliopilastoode_nouded.pdf);
- töö sisu vastavust õpieesmärkidele;
- töö vastavust vormistamise ja viitamise reeglitele;
- oma seisukohtade suulist kaitsmist.
Hinde kujunemisel võetakse arvesse samuti:
- juhendaja arvamust;
- retsensendi arvamust (kui kaitsmisel kasutatakse retsenseerimist);
- suulise kaitsmise taset.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: OIEO.04.140 | Nimi (ET): Uurimistöö | Nimi (EN): Research Paper | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Aaro Mõttus, Andra Laurand, Andreas Kangur, Andres Parmas, Andres Vutt, Annegrete Palu, Anneli Soo, Ants Nõmper, Gaabriel Tavits, Gea Lepik, Hesi Siimets-Gross, Irene Kull, Jaan Ginter, Janno Lahe, Katre Luhamaa, Lauri Mälksoo, Lea Leppik, Margit Vutt, Mario Truu, Marju Luts-Sootak, Martin Käerdi, Merike Ristikivi, Priit Kama, René Värk, Silvia Kaugia, Susann Liin, Tambet Grauberg, Triinu Rennu, Villu Kõve | Kirjeldus: Aine sisuks on kirjaliku uurimuse koostamine. Uurimistöö peab vastama õigusteaduskonna nõukogu poolt kinnitatud kirjalikele töödele esitatavatele nõuetele. 
1. Üliõpilase uurimustöö on üliõpilase poolt valitud teemal ja õppejõu juhendamisel koostatud kirjalik uurimus.
Uurimistöö teema valib üliõpilane kooskõlastatult juhendajaga kaitsmisele eelneval sügissemestril 15. oktoobriks.
2. Kirjalik uurimustöö peab vastama oma sisult ja mahult juhendava õppejõu poolt määratud nõuetele, sisaldama 6 EAP ulatuses iseseisvat tööd ning olema kirjutatud arvutitrükis 1,5-intervallise reavahega, 12-punktilise tähesuurusega, ca 2000 tähemärki leheküljel, Times New Roman'i kirjas (ligikaudne maht ca 20-25 lk). Kirjalike tööde esitamisel tuleb kinni pidada kehtestatud lõpptähtaegadest (vt akadeemiline kalender).
Juhendajaks võivad olla õigusteaduskonna õppejõud või isikud, kes on oma ala tunnustatud spetsialistid, ning kellel on vähemalt magistrikraad või sellele vastav haridustase.
Juhendaja võib väljastpoolt õigusteaduskonda olla ainult juhul, kui selleks on mõjuv põhjus. Välisjuhendaja kooskõlastab üliõpilase avalduse ja välisjuhendaja kirjaliku nõusoleku alusel osakonna juhataja. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Uurimistöö kaitsmise eelduseks on juhendaja nõusolek töö kaitsmisele lubamiseks.

Uurimistöö esitamine ja kaitsmine vastavalt akadeemilisele kalendrile.
Uurimis- ja magistritööde juhendamise kord, kättesaadav kodulehel https://oigus.ut.ee/sites/default/files/inline-files/loputoo_nouded_kaitsmiskomisjoni_moodustamise_kord_ja_kaitsmise_kord.pdf

III. Üliõpilase õigused ja kohustused
3.1. Üliõpilasel on õigus saada juhendajalt kokkulepitud aegadel töö kohta tagasisidet. Tagasiside mittesaamisel võib üliõpilane pöörduda instituudi juhataja või tema asetäitja poole.
3.2. Üliõpilane on kohustatud:
3.2.1. võtma juhendajaga omavahelise koostöö ning juhendamise ajakava kokkuleppimiseks ühendust hiljemalt ühe kuu jooksul alates töö teema valimise tähtpäevast;
3.2.2. osalema juhendaja korraldatud kokkusaamistel;
3.2.3. pidama kinni kokkulepitud töö koostamise tähtpäevadest. Kokkuleppe puudumisel tuleb magistritöö terviktekst esitada juhendajale vähemalt kaks kuud ning uurimistöö terviktekst vähemalt üks kuu enne töö esitamise tähtpäeva;
3.2.4. võtma töö kirjutamisel arvesse juhendaja instruktsioone;
3.2.5. vastama juhendaja kirjale või informeerima tagasiside saatmise ajast viie tööpäeva jooksul või hiljem, kui selleks on mõjuv põhjus;
3.2.6. esitama juhendajale tagasiside andmiseks keeleliselt korrektselt vormistatud teksti. | Hindamise meetod: Kaitsmine on hindeline (A-E).
Hinde kujunemisel arvestatakse:
- töö vastavust esitatud nõuetele (https://oigus.ut.ee/sites/default/files/inline-files/oigusteaduskonna_uliopilastoode_nouded.pdf);
- töö sisu vastavust õpieesmärkidele;
- töö vastavust vormistamise ja viitamise reeglitele;
- oma seisukohtade suulist kaitsmist.
Hinde kujunemisel võetakse arvesse samuti:
- juhendaja arvamust;
- retsensendi arvamust (kui kaitsmisel kasutatakse retsenseerimist);
- suulise kaitsmise taset.

opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course student
- After finishing the course students:
- can understand the essential in a familiar topic;
- can compile texts on a familiar topic or a topic interesting for the student both in the oral and written mode, and use the newly acquired grammatical structures in the right way;
- can describe experiences and plans, exchange important information and express their  opinion on practical problems;
- can participate in short conversations on everyday matters and in ordinary situations without prior preparation;
- can make social contact (greeting, saying good-bye, introduction, thanking, agreeing on a time to meet, etc.);
- can write short simple coherent texts.

- After completing the course the student
- - knows the main results about exponential family of distributions and their properties;
- - can find the maximum likelihood estimator and prove the main properties of the maximum likelihood estimator;
- - can describe the notions of sufficiency and completeness and find a sufficient statistic;
- - knows the concept of efficient estimator and conditions for its existence, knows the Cramer-Rao inequality and can prove the related results;
- - can find an efficient estimator for a parameter or its function;
- - knows the Neyman-Pearson hypotheses testing theory and the main results about uniformly most powerful tests, can construct the related test statistics;
- - has knowledge about different types of statistical dependence and association measures like Pearson, Spearman and Kendall coefficients, can estimate and interpret them.

- The student who has passed the lecture course:
- a) is aware of the general problems of interreligious theology as a discipline;
- b) points out basic keywords relevant in interreligious dialogue, discusses their relations and particular problems emerging from those relations;
- c) applies the above knowledge to give globally oriented theological meaning to actual topical events.

- After the course, the students are expected:
- * Knows the components of a personal computer;
- * Is capable to choose the appropriate settings for a given hardware;
- * Is capable to choose the appropriate power supply, hard disk or SSD, printer etc for a given computer system.
- * Knows the ARM architecture and Is capable to write simple programs in this;

- Student who pass the course:
- a) knows the main concepts of innovations;
- b) understands the theoretical and practical questions of innovations;
- c) knows how to relate innovation with other fields of economics and business administration;
- d) can evaluate which factors should be taken into account while generating innovative thinking in the company;
- g) has acquired skills for the holistic analysis of innovations;
- h) has obtained positive attitudes towards acceptance of versatile and novel perspectives in a company;
- i) is familiar with the main innovation problems in Estonian organizations and in a global context.

hindamise_meetod:
Kirjalik eksam testi vormis - 100 küsimust.
Teemad on farmaatsia instituudi koduleheküljel.
Hindamiskriteeriumid on järgmised:
A - suurepärane, ;
B - väga hea;
C - hea;
D - rahuldav;
E - kasin;
F - mitterahuldav.
Hindamise aluseks võetakse antud õppeaastal saavutatud parim tulemus (nt 92% võimalikust) ning hindepallid kujunevad saadud vahemiku (antud näites 51-92%) jagamisel viie hindepalli vahel võrdsete osadena. Juhul kui parim tulemus on väiksem kui 81%, võrdsustatakse parim tulemus 91%-ga.
Lõpueksami tulemuste hindamisel kasutatakse suhtelist skaalat, s.t maksimaalse saavutatud tulemuse ja minimaalse lubatud positiivse tulemuse (51 punkti) vahele jääv punktiskaala jagatakse viieks võrdseks osaks. Neisse vahemikesse jäänud punktisummad vastavad hinnetele A, B, C, D ja E. 50 või väiksema punktide arv vastab hindele "F"

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: ARFA.02.060 | Nimi (ET): Lõpueksam | Nimi (EN): Graduation Examination | EAP: 5.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: integreeritud bakalaureuse- ja magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: meditsiiniteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Ain Raal, Andres Meos, Daisy Volmer, Ivo Laidmäe, Jyrki Tapio Heinämäki, Karin Kogermann, Külli Jaako, Meeme Utt, Urve Paaver | Kirjeldus: Toimub kirjalik eksam testi vormis. Küsimused hõlmavad järgmisi distsipliine: farmakopöa analüüsimeetodid, farmatseutilist keemiat, farmatseutilisi abiained, raviainete metabolismi,  farmatseutilist tehnoloogiat (sh galeenilist farmaatsiat), biofarmaatsiat, sotsiaalfarmaatsia ja ravimite ohutust, farmakognoosiat, füüsikalist farmaatsiat, farmakoloogiat, farmakoteraapiat. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Eksamile pääseb, kui üliõpilasel pole mingeid võlgnevusi.
Kirjalik eksam (Moodle test). | Hindamise meetod: Kirjalik eksam testi vormis - 100 küsimust.
Teemad on farmaatsia instituudi koduleheküljel.
Hindamiskriteeriumid on järgmised:
A - suurepärane, ;
B - väga hea;
C - hea;
D - rahuldav;
E - kasin;
F - mitterahuldav.
Hindamise aluseks võetakse antud õppeaastal saavutatud parim tulemus (nt 92% võimalikust) ning hindepallid kujunevad saadud vahemiku (antud näites 51-92%) jagamisel viie hindepalli vahel võrdsete osadena. Juhul kui parim tulemus on väiksem kui 81%, võrdsustatakse parim tulemus 91%-ga.
Lõpueksami tulemuste hindamisel kasutatakse suhtelist skaalat, s.t maksimaalse saavutatud tulemuse ja minimaalse lubatud positiivse tulemuse (51 punkti) vahele jääv punktiskaala jagatakse viieks võrdseks osaks. Neisse vahemikesse jäänud punktisummad vastavad hinnetele A, B, C, D ja E. 50 või väiksema punktide arv vastab hindele "F"

opitulemused_en:
- A student
- - understands the formation of Ancient Greek and Roman literature;
- - is familiar with the literary genres and forms as well as the history of ancient literature;
- - has an overview of the most important authors and works of the Ancient Greek and Roman literature;
- - is aware of the ways how ancient literature influenced later European literatures.

- After passing the course student
- After finishing the course students:
- can understand the essential in a familiar topic (studies, working, free time etc.);
- can compile texts on a familiar topic or a topic interesting for the student both in the oral and written mode, and use the newly acquired grammatical structures in the right way;
- can describe experiences and plans, exchange important information and express their  opinion on practical problems;
- can find  necessary information from everyday texts and can understand the gist of  radio and TV programmes that are broadcast slowly and clearly, if these include familiar or interesting topics;
- can participate in short conversations on everyday matters and in ordinary situations without prior preparation;
- can make social contact (greeting, saying good-bye, introduction, thanking, agreeing on a time to meet, etc.)
- can write short simple coherent texts)

- Learners who have passed the course are able to:
- use the course vocabulary in context; 
summarize texts in spoken form.

- 1) has acquired the skill in reading of selected texts of the Pali canon and Mahayana in translation;
- 2) is able to analyse the text as well as read and expound its content;
- 3) can make associations between concepts and positions found in particular text with Buddhist doctrines in wider scope.

- A student who has completed the course:
- •	can name and recognize the key types of medieval buildings and artworks, as well as important individual works;
•	can describe the sources and methods used in the study of medieval art;
•	can explain the process of commissioning and producing art in the Middle Ages;
•	can analyze the connections between art, power, religion, self-representation, and other significant phenomena;
•	is proficient in and able to correctly use discipline-specific terminology;
•	is able to do teamwork.

- Upon successful completion of the course, the student:
- 1. understands the different aspects of medieval princely power, e.g., the lords' relations to his vassals and his towns, the practice of legal jurisdiction, the functioning of military service, and what changes occurred therein during the middle ages;
- 2. is familiar with the noble titles associated with princely power (emperor, king, archbishop, bishop, grand prince, prince, duke and margrave), and with the several ways of becoming a prince (primogeniture, dividing a principality between the heirs, una manu, and electing a prince);
- 3. is acquainted with medieval theories of the essence of princely power;
- 4. understands the terminology relevant to the study of the princely power in the Middle Ages, and employs it in scholarly practice;
- 5. has acquired competence in working individually with secondary sources;
- 6. has acquired an experience of reading and interpreting medieval written sources.

- After completion of the course the students will be able to
- 1) specify the symptoms and signs, epidemiology, etiology and pathogenesis of major internal diseases;
- 2) demonstrate practical skills in acquiring a complete history and physical examination of a medical patient;
- 3) differentiate between normal and pathology physical, laboratory and radiological findings in internal medicine
- 4) describe the major indications, adverse events, interactions and contraindications of commonly used drugs in the management of internal diseases

- After passing the course student
- Course will give students:
*	knowledge of different multivariate statistical methods, their application possibilities and interpretation of the gained results;
*	knowledge and skills of applying multivariate analysis using software packages;
*	skills and experiences to find suitable data for statistical data analysis, how to systemise and prepare data for multivariate analysis;
*	skills how to carry out parametric and non-parametric multivariate statistical analysis, interpret results of statistical data analysis, how to generalise findings to the research questions and how to present research results.

- On completing the course, the learners
- 1, describe how the needs of learners of different ages and varying levels of language proficiency can be addressed in the English language classroom, taking into account the principles of plurilingualism and pluriculturalism;
- 2. describe various classroom management challenges, propose solutions to them, and identify the advantages and limitations of the possible solutions;
- 3. identify a range of activities (including those based on ICT tools) and strategies that support the development of learners’ skills in completing oral and written receptive and productive activities, as well as in interaction and mediation;
- 4. identify and apply different approaches to correcting errors in oral and written work and techniques for dealing with learner errors;
- 5. analyse English language lessons based on the agreed criteria, suggesting possible activities for their further improvement;
- 6. critically read academic literature in the field of didactics, outlining the author’s main arguments and presenting and justifying their own position on the topic under discussion;
- 7. set goals and plan their further professional development by analysing their strengths and areas for improvement in a digital teaching portfolio.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
1. Osalemine tundides vähemalt 80% ulatuses;
2. Kontrolltööde (2) ja suulise eksami sooritamine vähemalt hindele E (51% õigeid vastuseid);
3. Kodutööde esitamine vähemalt 91% ulatuses.
4. Suulise eksami sooritamine vähemalt hindele E.

opitulemused_en:
- After the course, the students are expected:
- * to knew the essential rules of electrical safety;
- * to be able to use the multimeter for voltage, resistance and current measurements;
- * to be able to measure with oscilloscopes;
- * to be able to estimate the measurement uncertainty;
- * to be able to write the measurement reports with help of the spreadsheet programs;
- * to be able to explain the essential details of the measurements made.

- After completion of the course the students will be able to
- 1)specify the symptoms and signs, epidemiology, etiology and pathogenesis of major rheumatic diseases;
- 2) demonstrate practical skills in acquiring a complete history and physical examination of a rheumatic patients;
- 3) differentiate between normal and pathology physical, laboratory and radiological findings in rheumatic diseases
- 4) describe the major indications, adverse events, interactions and contraindications of commonly used drugs in the managment of rheumatic diseases
- 5) outline the health and economic impact and prognosis/outcome of musculosceletal conditions

- Students who pass the course:
- 1) know the basic concepts and implications of public sector economics;
- 2) can identify standard situations when government intervention into the economy is needed, know basic policy instruments that government has for intervention and can discuss their suitability in standard cases;
- 3) can analyse standard cases for government intervention and the main consequences of different policy instruments with the help of graphical models;
- 4) are able to analyse tax incidence and economic efficiency of taxes with the help of graphical models;
- 5) are able to evaluate critically the possibilities for practical implementation of different theoretical models and understand that there are no universal "best" solutions to problems

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Kummagi vahetesti tulemus vähemalt 51%; 
Kõik Moodle ülesanded sooritatud. 
Seminaridest osavõtu protsent vähemalt 75%, ehk siis võib puududa maksimaalselt neli korda.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course, the student:
- - names the main trends and developments of Norwegian, Swedish and Danish literary history up until the second half of the 20th century;
- - compares and analyses the literary traditions of Norway, Sweden and Denmark;
- - names the major authors and works in Scandinavian literature and introduces them to others.

- After taking the course a student:
- +++ can use Maxwell-Lorentz equations in 4-dimensional formalism with field strength tensor and dual field strength tensor; is able to determine how quantities describing the field and particles transform under Lorentz transformations and apply the transformations; know what are invariants of the electromagnetic field;
- ++ understands the correspondence between electromagnetic 4-potential and field strength, as well as the meaning of gauge freedom, gauge fixing, and gauge invariance; understands what is the number of degrees of freedom of the electromagnetic field;
- ++ knows the energy-momentum tensors of the electromagnetic field and relativistic particles; knows how energy, momentum, and angular momentum and their conservation are expressed via the energy-momentum tensor; understands how the conservation of energy, momentum, angular momentum, and electric charge are related to the underlying symmetries of the theory;
- + is able to derive the Maxwell-Lorentz equations in 4-dimensional formalism from the action functional;
- + is able to solve homogeneous wave equation for 4-potential, to obtain electromagnetic wave in terms of 4-dimensional polarization and wave vectors;
- + is able figure out how the electromagnetic wave is seen in different frames of reference (Doppler effect, light abberration)
- + understands the derivation of the field of arbitrarily moving charge (inhomogeneous wave equation, Lienard-Wiechert potentials);
- + knows what are advanced and retarded potentials and can interpret their meaning;
- + knows under which conditions will a moving charge radiate electromagnetic waves and can find the characteristics of the radiation;
- + knows the multipole expansion and the corresponding multipole moments of the electrostatic field and the field of stationary current;
- + can find the radiation field of slowly moving charges in dipole approximation.

