opitulemused_en:
- After the course the student:
-  is able to recognize critical illness of the patient;
-  is able perform primary management of critical conditions;
-  knows the organisation of emergency medicine, including triage at emergency
   department;
-  knows the primary management principles of severe trauma in hospital;
-  knows the principles of emergency surgery;
-  recognizes life-threatening arrhythmias and is able to treat them;
-  is able to perform cardio-pulmonary resuscitation of an adult;
-  is able to present the case history in short and concise way.

- After completing the course the student knows
- 1) the concept, content and history of plastic surgery;
- 2) subdivision of plastic surgery and its areas of usage;
- 3) types of wounds, wound healing;
- 4) treatment methods used in plastic surgery;
- 5) relying on gained knowledge the student is able to solve different problems concerning the surgery of skin and soft tissue.

- On completing the course a student will be able to:
- - demonstrate understanding of key areas of the differential psychology in educational context; childrearing and upbringing;
- - differentiate pupils' individual differences
- - have knowledge to dealing with individual differences;
- - analyse teachers&acute; possibilities in the process of the coping with different kinds of problems in relation to the pupils' individual differences.

- After completing the course the student knows
- 1) the epidemiology, etiology,pathogenesis and prophylaxis of more frequent surgical diseases;
- 2) the clinical picture and possible complications of surgical diseases;
- 3) contemporary clinical, laboratory and instrumental methods  of patient investigation;
- 4) treatment methods, incl operative treatment, and indications for their usage.
- The student is able to
- 1) take the anamnesis, carry out clinical examinations of a surgical patient and to analyse the results of general clinical tests;
- 2) draw up a plan for laboratory and instrumental examinations and analyse their results;
- 3) make clinical diagnosis, explain it on the basis of differential diagnosis;
- 4) determine indications for conservative or surgical treatment;
- 5) choose a method for operative treatment according to pathological changes.

- Student who has completed the practice:
- 1)  has experienced and practiced how to solve actual problems in IT law in technology startup companies;
- 2) Knows what the opportunities and challenges are working with technology startups on a position requiring legal education;
- 3) Has experienced and knows how to plan the work of a group, including has practiced leading a group;
- 4) Has developed communication skills.

kirjeldus_et:
Kursuse hõlmatav temaatika:
1. veebilehele kohustusliku õigusdokumentatsiooni analüüs;
2. interneti kaudu teenuslepingute sõlmimise põhiprintsiibid;
3. IKT dokumentide koostamise praktilised oskused;
4. IT lepingute põhiliigid;
5. IT lepingute sõnastamine, analüüs ja tingimuste läbirääkimine;
6. e-kaubanduse ja eraviisiliste internetitehingute peamised elemendid ja arengud (elektronandmevahetus ning arvutite ja arvutivõrkude varane kasutus erasektoris);
7. internetimüügi infoarhitektuur;
8. peamised ärimudelid (B2B, B2C, B2G jne);
9. tänapäeva e-kaubanduse mudelid ja trendid;
10. IT-ga seotud riigihangete õiguslikud ja tehnilised aspektid;
11. e-kaubandusele ja internetitehingutele kohalduvad rahvusvahelised ja regionaalsed õiguslikud režiimid;
12. e-kaubandusega seotud spetsiifilised probleemid: internetipangandus ja muud internetimaksete meetodid, tarbijakaitse; 
13. lepingutega seotud elektroonilise allkirjade õiguslikud aspektid;
14. infoühiskonna teenuste õiguslik regulatsioon.

kirjeldus_en:
The course covers:
1. Analysis of relevant legal documentation which must be present on a website;
2. Main principles of online contracting;
3. Development of practical skills for drafting ICT documentation;
4. Main types of IT contracts;
5. Formulating, analysing and negotiating IT contracts;
6. Main elements and evolutionary developments in the field of e-commerce and private online transactions (EDI and early private sector uses of computers and networks);
7. Information architecture of online sales;
8. Main business models (B2B, B2C, B2G etc.)
9. Contemporary e-commerce models and trends
10. Legal and technical aspects of IT related public procurements
11. International and regional legal regimes applicable to e-commerce and online transactions
12. Special issues related to e-commerce: online banking and other online payment methods, consumer protection 
13. legal aspects of electronic signatures in case of contracts
14. Regulation of information society services

