Students must work through the prescribed literature and tasks in order to prepare for lectures and seminars. Knowledge of the materials and the solutions of the tasks will be verified during the discussions held in the courses and seminars.
Individual work must be performed for both parts of the course in addition to attending lectures and seminars and working through the prescribed literature.
The objective of the individual work is to provide an assessment concerning the student's progress in the course.

Differentiated assessment will apply to individual work. The grade for the course will be formed of two components:
1. the two pieces of individual work to be performed within the framework of part E-Commerce of the course - 50% and
2. the two pieces of individual work to be performed within the framework of part IT-Contracts of the course - 50%.

Students must achieve at least 51% of the maximum grade in both parts of the course in order to pass. The individual work can get up to a total of 100 points.
A negative result in one part of the course will result in a negative total grade. A negative grade in one part of the course will not prevent passing the second part of the course.

kirjeldus_et:
Kursuse hõlmatav temaatika:

1.	autoriõiguse ja IKT vastandus;
        *	autoriõiguse põhiprintsiibid (sh tarkvara ja andmebaaside õiguslik kaitse);
        *	õiguste teostamine (nt vaba kasutus, digiõiguste haldus (DRM));
        *	autoriõigusega kaitstud teoste kasutamine (nt vastavalt seadusele, lepingule, Creative Commons'ile); tasulised ja tasuta tarkvaralitsentsid (BSD, GPL, MIT);

2.	tööstusomand;
        *	kaubamärkide ja domeeninimede õiguslike režiimide põhiprintsiibid;
        *	patendiõiguse, tööstusnäidiseõiguse jms põhiprintsiibid;

3.	intellektuaalomandi õiguse jõustamine infoajastul;
        *	praktiline teave intellektuaalomandi IT õigusega seotud kohtumenetlusest;
        *	riiklike ning rahvusvaheliste kohtute ja muude organite kohtupraktika (nt Euroopa Ühenduste Kohus);

4.	intellektuaalomandi- ja IT-õiguse tulevik;
        *	kõiki huvigruppe arvestaval mudelil põhineva Internetihalduse stabiilsus, õiguste halduse ja jõustamise võimalik edu või ebaõnnestumine jne.

opitulemused_en:
- The student will:
- * know the main legal concepts of intellectual property;
- * will be familiar with the relevant law applicable to IT related IP;
- * have necessary skills to assess the legal status of IT related intellectual property problem and is able to apply them;
- * be able to analyze and solve IT related intellectual property problems; apply these solutions and create legal strategies solo and in team.

hindamise_meetod:
The aspects of performance of the student that are assessed are the following (for the final result, all parts are added together):

- Written homework 1 (copyright): 20%;
- Written homework 2 (industrial property): 20%
- Test 20%;
- Moot Court submissions 20%;
- Moot Court oral participation 20%.
Level of positive performance ("E") is 51%.

