hindamise_meetod:
Peremeditsiini praktika on läbitud positiivsele tulemusele:
- kui on esitatud õigeaegselt iseseisva tööna patsiendi juhtumid, mis oleksid  õppejõudude poolt jälgitavad, suunatavad ning hinnatavad; 
- kui on vaja täiendada esitatud haigusjuhte, siis peab olema vastatud juhendaja poolt esitatud küsimusetele;
- esitatud praktika läbimise kohta päevik.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: MV00.00.005 | Nimi (ET): Peremeditsiini praktika | Nimi (EN): Family Medicine Practice | EAP: 12.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: integreeritud bakalaureuse- ja magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: meditsiiniteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Anneli Rätsep, Heli Tähepõld, Marje Oona, Ruth Kalda, Tarmo Loogus | Kirjeldus: Praktika eesmärgiks  on  aga  täiendada  õppuri  üldarstlikke  teadmisi,  tagamaks  tugevad  ning  laiad baasteadmised mis võimaldavad edasi õppida mistahes valitud erialal. Kliiniline praktika on eelnevalt täies mahus omandatud teoreetilisi teadmisi nõudev ja rakendav õppeaine. Kliinilise praktika raames on võimalus osaleda vastuvõtul ja lahendada sagedasemaid probleeme, millega patsiendid pöörduvad perearstikeskusesse, osaleda profülaktilise töö planeerimisel ja läbiviimisel ja teostada koduvisiite.
Perearstipraksises tuleb läbida 8 nädala pikkune peremeditsiini tsükkel. Peremeditsiinipraktikaks tuleb üliõpilasel endal sobiv praksis leida. Selleks sobib iga Eestis registreeritud  perearst  või  perearstikeskus  ning  välismaal  asuv  sarnase  profiiliga erialaesindaja või asutus. Peremeditsiini võib veel lisaks teha ka valiktsüklina ja   sooritamise  eelduseks  on  praktikabaasi nõusolek üliõpilane vastu võtta. 
Peremeditsiini  tsüklile  vastavad  seminarid  viiakse  läbi  elektroonselt Moodle õpikeskkonnas, kus tuleb valida ja analüüsida iseseisvalt 1 haigusjuht ja esitada kirjalikult aruteluks määratud töögrupis. Lisaülesanded on  täpsustatud päeviku vastava peatüki all. | Hindamise eeltingimused: E- seminaride läbimine on kohustuslik praktika osa! Patsiendi juhtumid peavad olema esitatud Moodle e-kursusel oma rühmale määratud tähtaja jooksul.  | Hindamise meetod: Peremeditsiini praktika on läbitud positiivsele tulemusele:
- kui on esitatud õigeaegselt iseseisva tööna patsiendi juhtumid, mis oleksid  õppejõudude poolt jälgitavad, suunatavad ning hinnatavad; 
- kui on vaja täiendada esitatud haigusjuhte, siis peab olema vastatud juhendaja poolt esitatud küsimusetele;
- esitatud praktika läbimise kohta päevik.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course, the student
- 1) can take anamnesis and examine patients objectively;
- 2) knows general principles of anti- and asepsis and can use them in practice;
- 3) can suture skin wounds and evaluate the healing process of skin wounds;
- 4) knows the basic symptomatology of and reasons for acute abdominal pain; can set up primary diagnosis for the patient with acute abdominal pain;
- 5) knows the basic principles of management of pre- and postoperative periods.
- 6) knows the basic principles of minor surgical procedures (treatment of superficial skin wounds, opening of abscesses, wedge resection of the nail)

hindamise_eeltingimused:
The grade is calculated from the total number of points (max 100). The points can be earned as follows:

1. Assignments (50 points): there will be ~10 assignments, each worth ~5 points;
2. Group project and presentation at the poster session (50 points);
3. Additional points can be earned from bonus tasks within assignments;

In order to pass the course, the student must get at least 50% from assignments (threshold 25 points), at least 50% from the project (threshold 25 points).

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: MTAT.03.239 | Nimi (ET): Bioinformaatika | Nimi (EN): Bioinformatics | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: doktoriõpe, magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: loodus- ja täppisteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Erik Abner, Kaur Alasoo, Priit Adler, Ralf Tambets | Kirjeldus: Kursus annab ülevaate bioinformaatikast - nii elementaarbioloogiast kui olulisematest bioinformaatika algoritmidest. Käsitletakse olulisemat bioloogilist ülesandepüstitust - DNA, RNA, valgud - järjestused, struktuur ja regulatsioon, geneetilised võrgustikud ja süsteemibioloogia. Käsitletakse uusi geenitehnoloogia meetodeid ja mahukaid uusi andmestike tüüpe. | Hindamise eeltingimused: The grade is calculated from the total number of points (max 100). The points can be earned as follows:

1. Assignments (50 points): there will be ~10 assignments, each worth ~5 points;
2. Group project and presentation at the poster session (50 points);
3. Additional points can be earned from bonus tasks within assignments;

In order to pass the course, the student must get at least 50% from assignments (threshold 25 points), at least 50% from the project (threshold 25 points). | Hindamise meetod: See https://courses.cs.ut.ee/

opitulemused_en:
- After passing this course every student knows:
- 1) methods of solution for simple 1. and 2. order partial differential equations
- 2) the classification of second-order partial differential equations;
- 3) the basic equations and typical problems of mathematical physics;
- 4) the methods for investigating and solving linear problems of mathematical physics.

kirjeldus_et:
Kursusel osalemise eelduseks on prantsuse keele teadmised Euroopa Nõukogu keeleoskustasemel A.1.1.
Semestris käsitletavad suhtlussituatsioonid ja sõnavara:
- ajakavast rääkimine, kellaaeg;
- kohtumise kokku leppimine;
- eluaseme kirjeldamine, toa reserveerimine hotellis;
- ruumiline paigutamine, teejuhatamine, kohtade kirjeldamine;
- kuuluvuse väljendamine;
- korralduste andmine;
- igapäevategevuste kirjeldamine, tänasest ja eilsest kõnelemine, minevikusündmuste edasiandmine;
- inimese kirjeldamine, välimus, rõivad, mood;
- esemete kirjeldamine (vorm, värv, materjal), valik, ostmine;
- toit, toidupoed, söögitavad, tellimine kohvikus või restoranis.
Grammatika:
- jätkuv töö tegusõnaga, ülevaade kindla kõneviisi aegadest, verbivormidest;
- küsilause struktuur, inversiooniga küsimus;
- demonstratiivid, kuuluvuse väljendamine possessiivi ja eessõna à abil;
- pronominaalne tegusõna;
- käsklause, il faut + infinitiiv;
- liitminevik passé composé;
- umbmäärane asesõna (quelqu'un, quelque chose) ja selle vasted eituslauses;
- kvantiteedi väljendamine, osaartikkel (du, de la, de l').

kirjeldus_en:
The course presupposes the Council of Europe Level A.1.1.
The contents of the course as communication situations and vocabulary related:
- talking about timetables, telling/asking the time;
- making an appointment;
- lodgings, booking a room;
- directions, describing views and places;
- expressing possession, describing one's belongings;
- giving orders;
- talking about everyday activities, today and yesterday, communicating past events;
- describing a person, his/her appearances, clothing, fashion; 
- describing different objects (their form, colour, material), choosing a gift, shopping;
- food, different food-stores, meals, ordering in a cafe/a restaurant.
Grammar topics:
- continuous verbe practice, general survey of the tenses of the indicative mood;
- interrogative sentence, questions with subject/verb inversion;
- demonstrative determiners, expressing possession (possessives + preposition à);	
- pronominal verbs;
- imperative mood, expression of obligation (il faut + infinitive);
- the past tense passé composé;
- impersonal pronouns (quelque chose, quelqu'un ) + negation: alternate forms (rien, personne);
- determiners: expressions of quantity, partitive articles.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: HVLC.03.008 | Nimi (ET): Prantsuse keele algkursus II (inglise keele baasil), tase A1.1 > A1.2 | Nimi (EN): French for Beginners II (on the Basis of English), Level A1.1 > A1.2 | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe, doktoriõpe, integreeritud bakalaureuse- ja magistriõpe, magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Reet Alas | Toimumisajad: Teisipäev, Neljapäev | Kirjeldus: Kursusel osalemise eelduseks on prantsuse keele teadmised Euroopa Nõukogu keeleoskustasemel A.1.1.
Semestris käsitletavad suhtlussituatsioonid ja sõnavara:
- ajakavast rääkimine, kellaaeg;
- kohtumise kokku leppimine;
- eluaseme kirjeldamine, toa reserveerimine hotellis;
- ruumiline paigutamine, teejuhatamine, kohtade kirjeldamine;
- kuuluvuse väljendamine;
- korralduste andmine;
- igapäevategevuste kirjeldamine, tänasest ja eilsest kõnelemine, minevikusündmuste edasiandmine;
- inimese kirjeldamine, välimus, rõivad, mood;
- esemete kirjeldamine (vorm, värv, materjal), valik, ostmine;
- toit, toidupoed, söögitavad, tellimine kohvikus või restoranis.
Grammatika:
- jätkuv töö tegusõnaga, ülevaade kindla kõneviisi aegadest, verbivormidest;
- küsilause struktuur, inversiooniga küsimus;
- demonstratiivid, kuuluvuse väljendamine possessiivi ja eessõna à abil;
- pronominaalne tegusõna;
- käsklause, il faut + infinitiiv;
- liitminevik passé composé;
- umbmäärane asesõna (quelqu'un, quelque chose) ja selle vasted eituslauses;
- kvantiteedi väljendamine, osaartikkel (du, de la, de l'). | Hindamise eeltingimused: 1) Aktiivne osavõtt õppetööst (vähemalt 75% st 20 korda).
2) Positiivne tulemus kontrolltööde (3) eest (60% õigeid vastuseid, kontrolltööde ajal ei ole lubatud kasutada õppe- ega muid lisamaterjale). Iga kontrolltööd saab järele teha ühe korra. Positiivsele tulemusele sooritatud kontrolltöö kordussooritus hinde parandamise eesmärgil ei ole lubatud.
3) Kõikide Moodle'i testide positiivsele tulemusele sooritamine.
4) Kodutööde nõuetekohane ja õigeaegne esitamine.
5) Kodulugemise vastamine "arvestatud" tulemusele. | Hindamise meetod: Kursusel kasutatakse pidevhindamist. Hinne saadakse kokkuvõtvalt aktiivse osalemise eest praktikumides, kodutööde esitamise, verbipööramise ja tekstimõistmise testide sooritamise, kodulektüüri eduka vastamise ja kolme kontrolltöö positiivse sooritamise põhjal. Eraldi eksamitööd ei kirjutata, kokkuvõttev hinne kujuneb kontrolltööde tulemuste aritmeetilise keskmisena.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course the student
- 1) has an understanding of the epidemiology, etiopathogenesis and risk factors of vascular surgical diseases;
- 2) has an overview of principles of diagnosis and treatment of more common vascular surgical diseases.

hindamise_meetod:
Kursuse lõpphinne kujuneb kolme komponendi põhjal:
1) Moodle's tehtavad testid -20% ;
2) lühiuurimus - 60% (referaat + selle tulemuste suuline lühiesitlus lõpuseminaris või salvestatud videoesitluse näol Moodle's); 
3) tagasiside kaasüliõpilase uurimustööle - 20%.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: FLGR.02.069 | Nimi (ET): Antiikaja olmekultuur | Nimi (EN): Greek and Roman Antiquities | EAP: 3.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Ivo Volt, Janika Päll, Kadri Novikov, Maria-Kristiina Lotman | Toimumisajad: Neljapäev | Kirjeldus: Kursus annab ülevaate Kreeka ja Rooma reaalidest, kombestikust, sotsiaalsetest suhetest, igapäevaeluga, hariduse ja kasvatusega seotud olustikust. Käsitletakse antiikaja elamut, sööke ja nõusid, perekonnaelu, haridust, muusikat, seltskondlikke ja perekondlikke tavasid, linnade infrastruktuuri ja ühisteenuseid. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Osalemine auditoorses/veebi teel toimuvas õppetöös, tutvumine Moodle's jagatud materjalidega. | Hindamise meetod: Kursuse lõpphinne kujuneb kolme komponendi põhjal:
1) Moodle's tehtavad testid -20% ;
2) lühiuurimus - 60% (referaat + selle tulemuste suuline lühiesitlus lõpuseminaris või salvestatud videoesitluse näol Moodle's); 
3) tagasiside kaasüliõpilase uurimustööle - 20%.

opitulemused_en:
- After the completion of the course, the student:
- - understands the main features of the historical and cultural-historical development in Denmark, Norway and Sweden;
- - summarizes and critically comments upon the course literature, and, proceeding from that, the main problems connected to the study of history of these periods;
- - presents the studied materials in the form of group work, compares these to each other and brings out commonalities and points of difference;
- - is able to analyse the connections and differences between cultural traditions in different Scandinavian countries, and sees their importance for getting an insight into modern society and mentality;
- - compares and analyzes the connections and differences in the history of the three Scandinavian countries.

- Upon completion of the course students:
- - know the difference between editing and proofreading;
- - use practical language  sources critically;
- - correct errors in adhering to the rules of Estonian literary standard and good practice;
- - give informed feedback and language advice:
- - analyse their prospects for working as language editors or proofreaders.

- After completing the course, the student:
- -	is able to take the anamnesis, examine patients with various internal diseases objectively, prescribe optimal diagnostic investigations and evaluate the results of the investigations;
- -	have learn general aspects common internal disease and able to analyse clinical symptoms of the disease and to establish final clinical diagnosis;
- -	knows the treatment algorithms and guidelines of long-term management of internal diseases;
- -	is able to present patient case to colleagues using appropriate medical terminology, to do necessary documentation and write an epicrisis (a critical or analytical summing up of a medical case history).

- On successful completion, the student:
- 1) can list example fields of robotics technology and explain the state-of-the-art in those fields;
- 2) can program ROS nodes using either C++ or Python;
- 3) is able to integrate existing ROS packages to a larger ROS-based project;
- 4) is familiar with and can describe the standard tools/packages of ROS, such as roslaunch, RViz, MoveIt!, Navigation, tf;
- 5) can implement ROS-based solutions for most common robotics problems, e.g., coordinate transformation, path-planning, inverse kinematics, and collision-free motion planning.

- After completing the course, the student
- - can describe prevention strategies of traumas and injuries;
- - can carry out a triage of the multitrauma patient;
- - can prioritize the stages of primary management of the multitrauma patient;
- - can describe the guidelines and methods to be used in primary stabilisation and final treatment of the multitrauma patient;
- - can identify how concomitant conditions, diseases and the mechanism of trauma influence primary treatment;
- - can describe and practise teamwork oriented management of the multritrauma patient at the primary level;
- - can plan transportation of the trauma patient for definitive treatment at a higher level hospital

- The student who graduated the course:
- - has an overview of basic concepts of organic chemistry and knows classification of human body biomolecules;
- - can name human body biomolecules by international (IUPAC) nomenclature;
- - knows basic concepts of structure and stereochemistry of human body biomolecules;
- - knows basic reactions occurring in human body;
- - knows structure of biomolecules (important metabolites, peptides, proteins, saccharides, lipids, nucleic acids) and also their biofunctions and biomedical importance;
- - knows structure and biomedical importance of biomembranes;
- - can orientate in basic terms of medical metabolomics and bioorganic chemistry, describe and discuss about structural features needed for certain biofunctionality of metabolites, high molecular weight biomolecules, and drugs.

- Student:
- - understands and follows the work ethic and organization of the practice base;
- - can do teamwork and analyze his/her role in it;
- - knows the peculiarities of the main diseases occurring in different fields and is able to independently apply their theoretical knowledge in practical activities;
- - independently and properly prepares a physiotherapy report using correct professional terminology;
- - evaluate and analyze the development of his/her professional knowledge and skills in practice.
- The practice is related to the parts of career planning such as self-analysis (eg ability to analyze and interpret professional experience), knowledge of possibilities (eg have an idea of the professional identity of professions related to their specialty) and planning (eg ability to plan their working time).

- After completion of the course, the student has knowledge about:
- -	the nature of the Continental-European legal culture;
- -	the origin of law;
- -	the nature and structure of legal norms and legal order;
- -	implementation of law as a part of the state power actions in realisation of law.
- The student:
- -	knows principles of functioning of the law;
- -	knows basic concepts of the observed disciplines;
- -	understands the relationships of the observed legal disciplines;
- -	understands the implementation of the general principles of law;
- -	can find and use principle sources of law.

- After finishing the course students are able to
1) characterise the essense and branch disciplines of physical geography;
2) know the main astronomical parameters and principles of the earth;
3) describe the structure and composition of the atmosphere;
4) know the main definitions of cartography and cartographic projections;
5) understand the main principles of geoinformatics and the possibilities or the use of remote sensing;
6) describe the elements of the radiation budget and heat budget of the earth;
7) understand the mechanism of the formation of wind and large-scale atmospheric circulation;
8) describe the mshanisms of the formation of precipitation main types of clouds;
9) discuss the problems of air pollution;
10) know the main air masses and fronts, different cyclones in the atmospheres;
11) describe the global climate system;
12) analyse the global water exchange and the elements of water budget;

- Learner who has completed the course:
- - knows the position of local self-government law in the Estonian legal order and is familiar with the most important legal acts and court practice in the field;
- - understands the impact of European Union law and international treaties concluded within the framework of the Council of Europe on local government law;
- - is familiar with the constitutional guarantees of local self-government and is able to analyse the most important objectives and principles of their implementation;
- - analyses current problems in local government law.

- After completion the student:
- - knows contemporary research results of the prevalence and factors affecting the risk, causes and course of mental disorders;
- - knows the psychological models of mental and psychosomatic disorders, and is able to explain the cognitive models of anxiety and psychosomatic disorders;
- - knows theories of stress;
- - knows the diagnostic criteria of common mental disorders;
- - is able to collect information about patient's symptoms, history of mental disorders and life history;
- - can explore and describe the mental status of patients; is able to recognise psychiatric conditions requiring emergency treatment;
- - knows the methods and aims of psychological assessment in different medical settings;
- - knows the possibilities of prevention, evidence based treatment and service organisation of mental disorders, knows the treatment principles and guidelines of major mental disorders;
- - understands the nature of evidence-based psychotherapy and knows the major schools of psychotherapy;
- - knows the principles of interpersonal communication, and is acquainted with skills supporting the interaction with the partner;
- - is able to use interviewing skills, including skills for active listening;
- - can impart information in a manner that enables patients to promote their health;
- - knows laws that regulate the treatment and rehabilitation of persons with mental disorders;
- - knows the ethical principles of working with people and problematic relationships that may arise in helping professions;
- - understands the nature and contributing factors of professional burnout;
- - knows the specific psychological features of working with children.

- After passing the course student
- - understands the role of the different speech organs in speech;
- - knows and explains the basic issues of phonetics, and makes connections between them;
- - knows and explains the basic terms of phonetics;
- - knows the basic symbols of the International Phonetic Alphabet;
- - finds relevant information in an article on the phonetic system, describes and compares the phonetic systems of different languages;
- - sets learning objectives and analyses him/herself as a learner, cooperates.

- On successful completion of the course, you will be able to
- - explain the composition of the social and political institutions in the English-speaking world and how they work (incl. in comparison to your country);
- - understand the social values and cultural traditions in today's English-speaking world;
- - compare the different English-speaking countries with each other and with their own country;
- - use the knowledge gained for the analysis of cultural texts from the countries studied;
- - analyse English-speaking societies in both written form and in oral presentations.

- After completing the course, the student
- 1) is able to take the anamnesis, examine patients objectively, prescribe optimal / supplementary diagnostic investigations and evaluate the results of the investigations.
- 2) in the case of cutaneous and subcutaneous infections, is able to analyse clinical symptoms of the disease and to establish final clinical diagnosis;
- 3) knows the etiopathogenesis, classification, clinical symtpomatology, diagnostic investigation methods and treatment algorithm of a disease;
- 4) has an understanding of the surgical treatment of presented diseases.

- After the course the student : 
- knows the most important differential diagnosis principles in family practice;
- is able to interpret the results of the most important laboratory analysis and other investigations used in family practice;
- knows to describe most important prevention methods in family practice;
- knows the core principles o f the management of the chronically ill patient;
- pharmacotherapy is able to assess the appropriateness of a particular patient;
- knows the principles of palliative care;
- is able to document clinically at general practitioner level and to plan outpatient admissions.

- The student will:
* identify and understand the different legal risks related to respective stages of an enterprise life cycle as every stage brings new challenges which require new approaches for successful resolution;
* understands connections between different IPR Intensive Enterprise life cycle parts and the relevant legislation;
* develop all necessary skills to assess and create legal strategies in support of various steps in an IPR Intensive Enterprise lifecycle;
* be able to define strategies to eliminate or minimise legal risks in each stage of the company.

hindamise_meetod:
