- 2) recalls radio measuring instruments purpose, parameters and can use these for basic measurements

- Upon successful completion of the course, the students will have developed the skills to:
- 1. understand and critically evaluate the pivotal events shaping the development of medieval legal systems;
- 2. identify the contemporary sources that underpinned legal thinking in the Middle Ages;
- 3. identify, assess and interpret sources of medieval legal history, understand and critically discuss the transformations and connections between different primary sources in their historical context;
- 4. understand contemporary legal terminology and employ it in scholarly practice;
- 5. coherently construct persuasive arguments from primary source material and articulate them in writing.

- A student successfully implemented internship:
