opitulemused_en:
- Kursuse läbinud üliõpilane:
- mõistab Põhjamaade kultuuritraditsiooni olulisemate protsesside laiaplaanilist tähendust;
- suudab analüüsida Põhjamaade kultuuriruumi iseärasusi ning
- esile tuua Põhjamaade panust maailma kultuurivaramusse; oskab iseloomustada ja analüüsida eri perioodide kultuurilisi ilminguid (sh kirjandus, kunst, teadus, filosoofia);
- omab ülevaadet Põhjamaade kultuuri- ja kunstiajaloo aktuaalsetest uurimisteemadest;
- on võimeline suulises ja kirjalikus vormis tutvustama läbitöötatud materjale ja iseseisva töö tulemusi.

- Upon completion of the course, the participating students will be able to:
- 1) understand the nature and transformation of intra-state and international conflicts;
- 2) explore and analyse the causal factors contributing to conflict escalation;
- 3) critically analyse the transformation of world order and international practice of interpreting legal principles on using the force;
- 4) use conflict management skills and methods for designing settlement options in conflict situations.

- A student 
- recognises grammar structures in written text in English and is able to find an adequate expression in Estonian;
- can use the present, the past and the future, commonly used prepositions, pronouns and articles;
- uses aqcuired knowledge in oral as well as written communication.

- Upon completion of the course, students should
- - be knowledgeable about the characteristics of academic texts;
- - be able to search for academic sources and read them for the purpose of assessing their relevance to their own research;
- - be familiar with stages in research (incl. academic writing) and capable of planning their time and activities accordingly;
- - create and format oral and written academic texts by applying knowledge and skills acquired during the course;
- - reflect on their writing habits and needs and assess needs for development;
- - analyse strengths and weaknesses in their MA thesis/project plans and organise their studies and research accordingly.

- Upon successful completion of the course, the student:
- * has necessary theoretical and methodological knowledge for writing a research paper on Estonian Intellectual History;
- * is able to conduct independent research and correctly formulate a research paper.

kirjeldus_et:
Üliõpilane viib kursust koordineeriva õppejõu juhendamisel läbi iseseisva praktika rakendades varem omandatud teadmisi rakendusantropoloogiast.  
Praktika raames üliõpilane:
- koostab koostöös ülikoolivälise partneriga uurimisprojekti plaani ja sõnastab praktika eesmärgid; 
- viib ülikoolivälise partneri juures läbi rakendusliku projekti;
- esitab kirjaliku praktikaaruande, milles analüüsib ja hindab kriitiliselt oma välitööde materjali, omandatud kogemust ja projekti raames ilmnenud eetilisi aspekte (s.h. kasutatud meetodeid ja nende rakendamist ja saadud tulemusi jm);
- esitab oma uurimuse tulemused ülikoolivälisele partnerile (kelle juures välitööd läbi viidi) sobivas vormis ja viisil.

kirjeldus_en:
Under the supervision the student is conducting an independent  practical project using knowledge related to applied cultural analysis.
The student:
-	is composing a research plan and aims of the study in collaboration with an external partner;
-	is conducting a practical project at an external partner;
-	presents a written work in which the collected materials, acquired experience and ethical issues are  critically analysed (e.g. methods and their application, the results etc.).
-	presents the final results of the study in a suitable media and form for the external partner.

