opitulemused_en:
- The student:
- - knows main aspects of strategic planning;
- - knows the basic terminology related;
- - is able to use various analyzing models;
- - knows the basic structure of strategies and is able to analyze it;
- - knows how to evaluate factors related to the implementation of strategies.

- Student who successfully completed the course
- - knows the history of Russian linguistics;
- - is able to orientate in the main issues of Russian linguistics;
- - knows the necessary Russian linguistic terms and is able to use them.
- - uses theoretical knowledge in further study;
- - knows how to conduct an academic discussion;
- - can critically analyze his / her language skills and speech usage.

- The student who graduated the course:
- - knows basic pathologic processes and mechanisms of development;
- - knows ethiology of the disorders of water and salt balance, acid-base balance, carbohydratis  and lipoprotein metabolism with main compensatory mechanisms in this case;
- - knows alterations in function and regulation of organs and systems during diseases.

- On successful completion, the student:
- knows why and where software defined radios are used;
- knows common building blocks and operating principles of software defined radios;
- can use GNU Radio to receive, transmit and filter radio signals;
- is familiar with the limitations of software defined radios and can take these limitations into account when designing a system.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) understands the development factors and expressions of the society and economy of welfare;
- 2) is aware of the concepts of health and well-being (welfare, wellbeing, wellness);
- 3) is aware of the principles of the concept of holistic wellness;
- 4) is able to critically analyse personal lifestyles, the determinants of wellbeing and opportunities for improvement;
- 5) is able to characterize and analyze products and services of wellness;
- 6) understands and analyzes specific aspects of health tourism business, i.e. health tourism products, services, establishments and destinations;
- 7) is able to group health tourists and describe their expectations, needs and wishes;
- 8) uses the principles of the concept of holistic wellness for the development of health tourism products, services and destinations.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
