- Upon completion of this course, the students:
- 1. are able to orient themselves in the main concepts and themes of Kant's aesthetics;
- 2. can relate these concepts to the main movements and developments in aesthetics and to the central issues in Kant's theoretical and practical philosophy.

- Student who has passed the subject:
- 1.	knows and uses space-related terminology;
- 2.	associates space topics with the syllabus of the taught subject;
- 3.	can compile tasks and use different study materials;
- 4.	plans and conducts practical work according to the curriculum and the age of the pupils;
- 5.	is aware of different ways to support learning;
- 6.	uses playful elements in the learning process.

- After passing the course student
- 1)	can plan and prepare lessons for special craft techniques in basic school based on the national curriculum and learners’ needs;
- 2)	will know special craft techniques, will compile a collection of methodological study material based on practical samples and will reflect on their learning and development.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) knows the processes of an accommodation enterprise;
- 2) understands the role of a manager in a service enterprise and its impact on organizational culture;
- 3) analyzes the stages of the visitor’s customer journey and the associated work processes;
- 4) analyzes the use of resources in an accommodation enterprise;
- 5) prepares service guidelines for an accommodation enterprise.

- By the end of the course the students acquire:
- 1. knowledge of the process of composing urban and regional plans;
- 2. an overview of the theoretical approach of spatial planning, the role of the planner and the legal system of Estonian planning
- 3. knowledge of the analyses necessary for planning, the ability to perform the most important spatial analyses;
- 4. an overview of visualisation and formal requirements of the spatial planning projects;
- 5. practical experience in developing a planning proposal;
- 6. skills to conduct a public consultation of the plan and to use participatory planning methods to involve stakeholders.

- Upon completing the course a student:
- 1) knows the principles of contemporary spatial planning and is able to discuss them from different cultural contexts;
- 2) is able to use relevant datasets for analyzing social-spatial processes and for preparing spatial plans;
- 3) has an overview of the main quantitative and qualitative methods used in spatial planning;
- 4) has skills for academic writing;
- 5) is able to select and apply appropriate GIS and visualization tools for spatial planning;
- 6) is able to develop general planning solutions (explanatory text and maps) based on analysis;
- 7) is able to compile spatial plan and design planning maps;
- 8) understands the concept of participatory planning and is able to select appropriate involvement methods;
- 9) has  skills to conduct a public discussion and to introduce publicly the planning solutions;
- 10) has participated in group work in international team.

hindamise_meetod:
Maximum 100 points can be received. 
The grade consists of several group-works, presentations and individual assignments:
Phase 1 (5%, 5 points): overview of the planning area & aim and vision of the plan (group assessment), analysis of spatial mobility plans  (individual assessment), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)
Phase 2 (45%, 45 points): empirical study (30 points, group assessment), individual conversation (15 points, individual assessment),  review (presentation and submission of written document) of other group's work (pass/fail, group assessment)), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)
Phase 3 (50%, 50 points): planning project (30 points, group assessment), spatial plan map(s) (20 points, individual assessment), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)

A: 91-100 points, B: 81-90 points, C: 71-80 points, D: 61-70 points, E: 51-60 points, F: 0-50 points.

In phase 1 we evaluate:
1) overview of the planning area & aim and vision of the plan;
2) analysis of spatial mobility plans;

In phase 2 final study report we evaluate:
1) introduction and conclusions; 
2) theoretical overview; 
3) data and methods; 
4) results;
5) discussion;
6) formatting;
7) defence: final presentation and discussion.

In phase 3 planning project we evaluate:
1) substantive adequacy;
2) the use of different visualisation methods and techniques;
3) the development of the plan during the course;
4) formatting;
5) presentations and defence;
6) spatial plan map

Regarding the presentation we evaluate:
- structure of the presentation and presentation of the case,
- argumentation,
- justification of chosen viewpoints and solutions.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: LTOM.02.010 | Nimi (ET): Planeerimise projekt | Nimi (EN): Planning Project | EAP: 15.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: inglise keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: loodus- ja täppisteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Ago Tominga, Ingmar Pastak, Pille Metspalu, Raul Garcia Estevez, Siiri Silm | Kirjeldus: Tudengid tutvuvad erinevate planeerimisteooriate ja meetoditega ning rakendavad neid teadmisi planeerimisprojektis grupitööna. Oluline osa grupitööst on õppida tegema koostööd ja osalema kommunikatsiooniprotsessis planeeringute koostamisel. Iga rühma planeerimisprojekti üldine teema on paika pandud õppejõudude poolt. Kursuse käigus tehakse välitöid ja toimub planeeringulahenduse avaliku arutelu simulatsioon, lõpus kaitstakse välja töötatud planeeringulahendust. Kursus on jaotatud kolme etappi (ruumilise planeerimise teoreetiline kontekst, analüüs, planeeringulahenduse ja -kaardi koostamine), mida annavad erinevad õppejõud. Statisilise analüüsi tulemusi õpitakse kasutama planeeringulahenduse põhjendusena.
1. Planeerimise olemus Lääne maailma kontekstis.
Esimeses etapis omandavad tudengid teadmisi planeerimise olemusest ja aktuaalsematest ruumilise planeerimise teemadest (nt jätkusuutlikkus, mobiilsus jm). Lisaks tutvutakse uurimisaluse piirkonna oluliste teemade, regulatsioonide ja planeeringutega. Töö käigus leitakse sobivad teoreetilised lähtekohad planeerimisprojekti lahendamiseks. Esimese etapi lõpuks sõnastatakse iga grupi/töörühma planeerimisprojekti peaeesmärk ja lähteülesanne.
2. Statistiline analüüs.
Teises etapis teostab iga grupp kvantitatiivse analüüsi, mis lähtub etteantud planeeringuprojekti teemast. Selleks kasutatakse statistilisi andmeanalüüsi meetodeid. Eesmärgiks on läbi viia empiiriline andmeanalüüs, et selle tulemusi rakendada planeerimisülesandes. Teise etapi lõpus esitavad tudengid enda analüüsi tulemusi.
3. Planeeringulahenduse koostamine
Kolmandas etapis töötatakse välja planeeringulahendused ja poliitikasoovitused põhinedes planeerimisprojekti lähteülesandele ja teostatud analüüsile. Koostatakse planeeringukaart koos seletuskirjaga.

NB! Eelnev kogemus GIS tarkvaraga (QGiS või ArcGIS) on vajalik. | Hindamise eeltingimused: All presentations must be delivered. At least 51% of points must be obtained from each phase of the course. | Hindamise meetod: Maximum 100 points can be received. 
The grade consists of several group-works, presentations and individual assignments:
Phase 1 (5%, 5 points): overview of the planning area & aim and vision of the plan (group assessment), analysis of spatial mobility plans  (individual assessment), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)
Phase 2 (45%, 45 points): empirical study (30 points, group assessment), individual conversation (15 points, individual assessment),  review (presentation and submission of written document) of other group's work (pass/fail, group assessment)), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)
Phase 3 (50%, 50 points): planning project (30 points, group assessment), spatial plan map(s) (20 points, individual assessment), individual contribution (pass/fail, individual assessment)

A: 91-100 points, B: 81-90 points, C: 71-80 points, D: 61-70 points, E: 51-60 points, F: 0-50 points.

In phase 1 we evaluate:
1) overview of the planning area & aim and vision of the plan;
2) analysis of spatial mobility plans;

In phase 2 final study report we evaluate:
1) introduction and conclusions; 
2) theoretical overview; 
3) data and methods; 
4) results;
5) discussion;
6) formatting;
7) defence: final presentation and discussion.

In phase 3 planning project we evaluate:
1) substantive adequacy;
2) the use of different visualisation methods and techniques;
3) the development of the plan during the course;
4) formatting;
5) presentations and defence;
6) spatial plan map

Regarding the presentation we evaluate:
