opitulemused_en:
- Upon completing the course, the student:
- explains the principles and application areas of ecotechnology and nature-based solutions;
- describes and compares eco-technological solutions in water, energy and building sectors, as well as in ecosystem restoration and environmental protection;
- evaluates and is able to select appropriate eco-technological and nature-based solutions for preventing and solving environmental problems;
- analyses scientific articles in the field of ecotechnology, formulates key conclusions and communicates them clearly;
- develops, in group work, eco-technological solutions suitable for urban environments and justifies their implementation;
- applies methods learned during field excursions and relates field observations to theoretical concepts.

- After completing the practice, the student is able to:
- know the components of the practice (work environment, supervisor, contract, report of the practice, feedback); 
- make a time schedule and manage time;
- gain experience in collecting, systemizing and analyzing information;
- describe and analyze the experience of the practice;
- gain experience in team work and develope communication skills;
- gain primary skills for integrating ICT-skills with humanities in the work environment;
- value the practice as a part of the study process;

- After successful completion of the course the student:
- - understands the basics of the applied folkloristics as a field of activity;
- - knows the major fields of applied folkloristics in contemporary Estonia;
- - knows main approaches and methods used in applied folkloristics;
- - is able to formulate a feasible idea how to use folkloristic knowledge and skills outside academia and is aware of various aways how to present this idea;
- - is familiar with major problems that may arise in the field of applied folkloristics.

- After passing this course every student:
- 1. is able to use vectors and operations of a vector algebra for solving simple problems;
- 2. recognizes the equations of straight lines, given sufficient geometrical data a student is able to find the equation of a straight line, he is also able to determine the mutual positions of two lines in the space and to calculate the distance from a line to a point and the angle between two lines;
- 3. recognizes the equations of planes, given sufficient geometrical data a student is able to find the equation of a plane in Cartesian coordinates; he is also able to determine the mutual positions of a line and a plane and two planes in a space, to calculate the distance from a plane to a point and the angle between a line and a plane and between two planes.
- 4. chooses suitable mathematical conceptions (formulae) for problems, and applies these conceptions while solving problems.

- Upon completion of the course students
- a) have improved their ability to communicate in one foreign language;
- b) can analyze their own language skills and needs as well as that of their tandem partner's and can plan cooperational language learning activities in a tandem;
- c) can give oral feedback to their tandem partners about the improvement of their language skills during the tandem course and analyze the feedback given to them;
- d) are more aware of the characteristics of intercultural communication and their strengths and weaknesses in it;
- e) having knowingly and purposefully planned their studies at the tandem course, can evaluate their cooperation, communication and time management skills.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) understands the self-management ideas and aspects;
- 2) understands specifics of human behaviour;
- 3) understands vitality, its different levels and importance on human health;
- 4) understands the possibilities for successful stress management;
- 5) can apply various techniques in self-management;
- 6) can follow a healthy lifestyle;
- 7) can implement techniques of self-management and stress management.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) identifies and describes the structure, core functions, and daily operations of the traineeship organisation within the tourism sector;
- 2) observes and analyses key service processes in the organisation, using a service-oriented mindset and relevant theoretical concepts;
- 3) recognises the organisation's main customer groups, services, and products, and reflects on how they meet customer needs and expectations;
- 4) reflects on their own learning experience, including professional behaviour, communication, and initial teamwork skills in a tourism context;
- 5) uses appropriate tourism-related terminology and academic sources when compiling the traineeship report;
- 6) presentation and defence of the traineeship experience.

- Student who pass the course:
- a) knows the key concepts within international entrepreneurship (IE),  innovation economics and innovation management; understands the main theories and research traditions in international business (IB) and in international entrepreneurship; is able to read and critically evaluate research in IB and IE and select appropriate frameworks for her/his research;
- b) understands the theoretical and practical questions of entrepreneurship and innovation of a company, from the co-operational, employee and manager perspectives;
- c) knows how to relate entrepreneurship and innovation with other fields of business administration and economics;
- d) can evaluate which factors and how affect innovation process of a firm;
- e) understands  the effects of innovation at the firm and at the aggregate economy level;
- f) knows how to apply main methods of business analysis; has an overview of the main methods applied in the empirical research of the determinants and effects of innovation;
- g) has acquired skills and experiences for the analysis of holistic functioning of entrepreneurial and innovation processes;
- h) has obtained positive attitudes towards acceptance of versatile and novel perspectives in entrepreneurial activities;
- i) is familiar with innovation problems in Estonian organizations and in a global context.

- Upon completion, course participants
- -	are familiar with key characteristics of the contemporary security environment;
- -	are able to name, describe, apply central concepts of the field of Security Studies;
- -	are familiar with, and are able to assess, central debates/arguments in the field of Security Studies;
- -	are able to apply key concepts of the field of Security Studies in order to critically analyze current security challenges.

- After the course, the student:
- 1.	Applies the scientific method to solve theoretical and experimental problems encountered in the field of study;
- 2.	Explains the connections between physics as a basic science and their field of study;
- 3.	Understands the self-organizing nature of life and other complex processes;
- 4.	Knows the basic laws of classical mechanics, quantum mechanics and thermodynamics and can use them to interpret and solve various situations;
- 5.	Understands the physical principles of the operation of various devices and takes them into account when using and improving the device.

- After passing the course student
- The student: 
- understands parties and their connections in the youth work field;
- analyses different professional identities in the youth field; 
- analyses networking in the youth field;
- plans cooperation with stakeholders in the field, including the necessary new forms of cooperation; 
- evaluates networking by applying own knowledge and skills.

- After completion the student:
- knows the diagnostic criteria of four groups of more common mental disorders;
- is able to collect information about patient's symptoms,history of four more common groups of mental disorders and their life history;
- can explore and describe the mental status of patients; is able to recognise psychiatric conditions requiring emergency treatment.

hindamise_meetod:
Kursuse lõputest arvestatud.
Aine läbimiseks teab üliõpilane rahuldaval tasemel alljärgnevat:
- teab psüühikahäirete psühholoogilisi ja bioloogilisi tekkepõhjuseid;
- tunneb nelja sagedasema psüühikahäirete grupi  (psühhoaktiivsetest ainetest tingitud, psühhootiliste, meeleoluhäirete, ärevushäirete) diagnoosikriteeriume ja antud häirete baaspsühhopatoloogiat;
- oskab koguda informatsiooni patsiendi kaebuste, haigus- ja eluanamneesi kohta;
- oskab hinnata ja kirjeldada psüühilist seisundit, sealhulgas ära tunda vältimatut psühhiaatrilist abi vajavad patsiendid;
- oskab hinnata patsiendi suitsiidohtlikkust ja suudab antud patsienti käsitleda.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: ARPS.01.082 | Nimi (ET): Erakorraline psühhiaatria I | Nimi (EN): Emergency Psychiatry I | EAP: 1.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: integreeritud bakalaureuse- ja magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristamata (arv, m.arv, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: meditsiiniteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Innar Tõru, Sven Janno, Vaiko Veikat | Toimumisajad: Kolmapäev | Kirjeldus: Annab ülevaate nelja sagedasema psüühikahäirete grupi psühhopatoloogiast, diagnostikast ja ravist. | Eeldusained: (ARFR.02.037 "Farmakoloogia ja toksikoloogia") | Hindamise eeltingimused: Kõigi loengute kuulamine. | Hindamise meetod: Kursuse lõputest arvestatud.
Aine läbimiseks teab üliõpilane rahuldaval tasemel alljärgnevat:
- teab psüühikahäirete psühholoogilisi ja bioloogilisi tekkepõhjuseid;
- tunneb nelja sagedasema psüühikahäirete grupi  (psühhoaktiivsetest ainetest tingitud, psühhootiliste, meeleoluhäirete, ärevushäirete) diagnoosikriteeriume ja antud häirete baaspsühhopatoloogiat;
- oskab koguda informatsiooni patsiendi kaebuste, haigus- ja eluanamneesi kohta;
- oskab hinnata ja kirjeldada psüühilist seisundit, sealhulgas ära tunda vältimatut psühhiaatrilist abi vajavad patsiendid;
- oskab hinnata patsiendi suitsiidohtlikkust ja suudab antud patsienti käsitleda.

hindamise_meetod:
