opitulemused_en:
- Those who have completed the course are expected to be able to:
- - understand and distinguish between the practice- and experience-based and, on the other hand, the theoretical and conceptual in the educational discussion; consciously operate between these two levels in their written and oral texts;
- - know and understand the reasons, the main developmental characteristics and the identity issues of general education as a discipline of its own; know and understand the traditional disciplinary and theoretical specificities of educational science in the English-speaking, the Continental European and the Nordic cultural spaces; understand and purposefully apply these specificities in their reading and writing;
- - distinguish, understand and critically assess the presence, the extent and the quality of a specifically educational component in written and oral scientific production;
- -  distinguish, understand and critically assess the degree of generality of a particular educational problem or topic; distinguish between the general educational and the field specific matter;

- After passing the course students will:
- analyse cientific articles written in Spanish, distinguishing research questions, theoretical frameworks and used methods in order to assess their appropriateness for investigating the linguistic phenomena at hand;
- apply the methods of analysis used in literature reviewed (e.g., data observation, text analysis, corpus analysis, experimental design) in small-scale practical assignments, interpreting the results in the context of the structure and use of Spanish;
- develop a personal position on linguistic phenomena and justify it, using academic articles discussed in class; participate in academic discussions on Spanish linguistics in an argumented way;
- reflect upon the strengths and limitations of linguistic research strategies and reason regarding the potential of different approaches (formal, functional, cognitive, sociolinguistic, discourse analysis, experimental) for understanding and explaining the variation and use of the Spanish language.

- Students knows how to work in the research laboratory/or enterprise, has acquired practical experience in the research field, got experience in both independent and team work.
- After the completion of the practice students:
- 1.	Is able to critically evaluate scientific literature, search and collect necessary data, make hypothesis based on the collected info;
- 2.	Is able to plan his/her work;
- 3.	Is able to work both in team and individually;
- 4.	Has skills to collect experimental data, analyse, format and present the results in oral and written form;
- 5.	Has passed the practice in research laboratory or enterpise, has tried the researcher role;
- 6.	Has gotten practical experience in the study field, which enables to make more informed career decisions;

- After the course, the student will:
- 1) apply their knowledge of physics to describe, explain and predict natural phenomena to level I and II students;
- 2) conduct experiments to demonstrate and explain physical phenomena;
- 3) plan experimental inquiry and ask questions related to the observed phenomena;
- 4) see the value of using hands-on experiments to explain natural phenomena.

- After passing this course the student:
- 1. is familiar with basic concepts related to divisibility (divisibility, gcd, lcm, prime number), knows and can prove their main properties; in particular, can use the Euclidean algorithm and the sieve of Erastothenes, and can solve the equation ax+by=c;
- 2. knows the notion of congruence and its fundamental properties, can prove those properties; in particular, can derive certain divisibility rules;
- 3. is familiar with the notion of residue class ring, knows which elements of such rings are invertible;
- 4. knows basic number theoretical functions, can compute with them and is able to prove some fundamental results about them;
- 5. is able to solve congruences; use and prove the Chinese Remainder Theorem.

