opitulemused_en:
- After passing this course every student
- 1.recognizes main concepts of general topology and is able to describe these in noncomplicated cases;
- 2.is able to make sure which complect σ of subsets of a set X defines a topology on X such that σ is a base of this topology, and which  does not;
- 3.knows what is the subset topology, the quotient topology and the product topology and is able to describe main concepts (as closed set, closure of a set and accumulation points of a set) in these topologies;
- 4.knows equivalent conditions for the continuity of map and is able to use these in noncompli-cated cases;
- 5.knows what means the homeomorphism and perceives the importance of this in topology;
- 6.knows what is the (directed) net and what can be described by nets in topology;
- 7.knows most important topological spaces and their properties;
- 8.knows why we need to extend topological spaces, what means the one-point compactifi-cation of a topological space and how to describe the topology of such compactification;
- 9.knows properties of compact spaces and understands the importance of such spaces in mathematics;
- 10.knows which topological spaces are connected and separable and knows main properties of these spaces.

- After having completed this course, students will be able to:
- - Explain how changes in government and governance, and technological innovations are related;
- Describe components of digital systems and digitalisation, and compare and evaluate various methodologies for the design and implementation of digital systems;
- Identify financial, legal and organizational challenges in relation to digitalisation; and
- Compare digital innovations and institutional changes in various national contexts.

- a) The knowledge of morphological and ecological characteristics of insect orders occuring in Estonia to the level when the participant is able to connect the majority of the local insects met in the field with the right insect orders and with particular habitats;
- b) The skill set of how to identify the local insects and mollusc species and the ability to determine some of  the most usual and easily recognisable insect and mollusc species without using the keys;
- c) The skill set of how to apply some of the most widespread collecting and preparing methods;
- d) The knowledge of how to use the software and store & publish the occurence data in public occurence data databases by using PlutoF (https://plutof.ut.ee/) platform as an example.

- A student who has passed the course:
- knows the general principles of editing specialised texts;
- knows how to use terminological databases;
- recognises errors that occur more often in specialised texts and makes the necessary changes by using language resources;
- knows the principles of plain language;
- knows how to explain the changes made during editing.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) knows the subjects and distribution of the financial environment;
- 2) applies the time value of money in solving the tasks;
- 3) assesses the value, return, and risk of securities;
- 4) knows the terminology and services provided of commercial banking;
- 5) knows the terminology and services provided of investment banking;
- 6) solves simple monetary situations encountered in commercial banking mathematically in Excel;
- 7) assesses financial investment returns, costs, profits, profitability, and taxes.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- - knows and is able to use basic concepts related to information systems and databases and knows how they relate (also open data, big data);
- - knows about information systems role in modern organization;
- - is able to name basic problems related to information systems privacy issuses and ethics;
- - knows about information system types which help to support organizations main processes and knows their general operational logic;
- - knows about information system types which help to support organizations support processes and knows their general operational logic;
- - knows what is organizations IT infrastructure, knows how to describe its functioning and management;
- - knows about information systems development process, how it affects the organization, and what to consider while implementing information systems;
- - knows what is state information system information architecture and why it is important;

- Upon successful completion of the course, the student:
- * understands the historical origins and the philosophical foundations of the concepts 'state' and 'sovereignty,' and grasps the multifaceted meanings of sovereignty in contemporary political philosophy;
- * can link the concept of sovereignty to current debates on issues related to political legitimacy and international order.
- More specifically, the student:
- * Has obtained a systematic understanding of the ideas of sovereignty and the state in the history of political thought;
- * Has acquired knowledge of the most important political philosophers and key texts in the debates about state and sovereignty;
- * Has acquired the capacity to see the broad way in which the fundamental assumptions about the nature of sovereignty are framing contemporary debates on legitimacy and international order;
- * Has acquired the capacity to debate the causes of and potential solutions to political and international crises through the prism of the conceptualizations of sovereignty and state power;
- * Has acquired the ability to analyze texts belonging to the history of political thought, taking into account their historical context;
- * Has improved the ability of critical thinking and the capacity to express ideas clearly in writing and oral discussions;
- * Has applied critical thinking about sovereignty to real-world challenges in contemporary politics.

- After the course, the students are expected to:
- 1. Know main differences between classical, relativistic and quantum physics;
- 2. Be able to calculate the apparent and real relativistic lengths of bodies, the durations of processes, the intervals between events, relativistic momenta and energies;
- 3. Be able to explain the following concepts: de Broglie waves, uncertainty relation, probability density, operator, expectation value, quantum state, eigenfunction, eigenvalue;
- 4. Know the thermodynamic parameters, thermodynamic potentials and correlations between those;
- 5. Be able to explain the concept of distribution function;
- 6. Know the Maxwell-Boltzmann, Fermi-Dirac and Bose-Einstein distribution functions and to be able to use them in the simplest cases.

hindamise_meetod:
Üliõpilasel tuleb teadmiste ja oskuste kontrolli käigus sooritada kokku 6 hindelist harjutust.
Need on:
1) Relativistliku füüsika (RF) põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 15 p);
2) Relativistliku füüsika (RF) ülesannete lahendamine (kuni 20 p);
4) Kvantfüüsika ülesannete kontrolltöö (kuni 20 p); 
Kvantfüüsika kontrolltööd on võimalik aine Moodle'i pesas harjutada. 
5) Kvantfüüsika põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 25 p);
6) Termodünaamilise protsessi graafikute teisendamine Vp-teljestikust TV- ja TS-teljestikesse (10 p);
7) Statistilise füüsika (SF) põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 10 p).
Kokku 15 + 20 + 20 + 25 + 10 + 10 = 100 punkti.

Juhul kui õppeaine läbitakse kontaktõppes, on lisaks üks nõutavatest ülesannetest aine põhivara tundmise lünktest (kuni 15 p).
Sel juhul väheneb kvantfüüsika osakaal 10 p võrra ja relativistliku füüsika osakaal 5 p võrra, võrreldes eelkirjeldatuga.
Positiivse koondhinde saamiseks tuleb koguda üle 50 punkti. Samuti tuleb kõik harjutused sooritada positiivsele hindele, st saades vähemasti pooled punktid maksimaalsest võimalikust. Hindeliste harjutuste sooritamise järjestus pole oluline. Niipea, kui on tekkinud valmisolek midagi sooritada, tuleb sellest õppejõule teada anda ning soorituskatse aeg kokku leppida.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: LOFY.01.114 | Nimi (ET): Kaasaegne füüsika | Nimi (EN): Modern Physics | EAP: 4.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: loodus- ja täppisteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Kalev Tarkpea, Kristjan Kalam | Kirjeldus: Kursuse alguses käsitletakse relativistliku füüsika ja kvantfüüsika peamisi erinevusi klassikalisest füüsikast. Seejärel omandavad üliõpilased oskuse selgitada eelistatult tavakeele sõnadega relativistliku füüsika ja kvantfüüsika põhimõisteid ning õpivad arvutama tähtsamaid relativistlikus füüsikas ja kvantfüüsikas kasutatavaid suurusi. Lõpuks tutvuvad üliõpilased analoogiliselt ka termodünaamika ja statistilise füüsika põhimõistetega. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Eritingimused puuduvad | Hindamise meetod: Üliõpilasel tuleb teadmiste ja oskuste kontrolli käigus sooritada kokku 6 hindelist harjutust.
Need on:
1) Relativistliku füüsika (RF) põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 15 p);
2) Relativistliku füüsika (RF) ülesannete lahendamine (kuni 20 p);
4) Kvantfüüsika ülesannete kontrolltöö (kuni 20 p); 
Kvantfüüsika kontrolltööd on võimalik aine Moodle'i pesas harjutada. 
5) Kvantfüüsika põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 25 p);
6) Termodünaamilise protsessi graafikute teisendamine Vp-teljestikust TV- ja TS-teljestikesse (10 p);
7) Statistilise füüsika (SF) põhideede esitamine õpilasele arusaadavas sõnastuses (kuni 10 p).
Kokku 15 + 20 + 20 + 25 + 10 + 10 = 100 punkti.

Juhul kui õppeaine läbitakse kontaktõppes, on lisaks üks nõutavatest ülesannetest aine põhivara tundmise lünktest (kuni 15 p).
Sel juhul väheneb kvantfüüsika osakaal 10 p võrra ja relativistliku füüsika osakaal 5 p võrra, võrreldes eelkirjeldatuga.
Positiivse koondhinde saamiseks tuleb koguda üle 50 punkti. Samuti tuleb kõik harjutused sooritada positiivsele hindele, st saades vähemasti pooled punktid maksimaalsest võimalikust. Hindeliste harjutuste sooritamise järjestus pole oluline. Niipea, kui on tekkinud valmisolek midagi sooritada, tuleb sellest õppejõule teada anda ning soorituskatse aeg kokku leppida.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course a student should be able to:
- -exchange essential information and express an opinion on familiar topics;
- -understand and use the acquired grammar and vocabulary in mono- and dialogues;
- -describe her everyday activities, speak about herself and get information from her conversation partner in usual conversations;
- -write simple texts about herself.

- Student who has completed the course:
- 1) has in-depth knowledge of solving cases including the fields of private, public and criminal law;
- 2) solves complex cases in a methodically correct manner, presenting systematic, comprehensive and accurate solutions, using correct Estonian legal language;
- 3) use the relevant legal provisions, relevant case-law and literature in solving the complex cases;
- 4) presents reasoned, logical and coherent positions in the resolution of complex cases;
- 5) is familiar with the current legal problems in the three areas, is able to identify them when solving various cases and to analyse them in depth and critically.

- By the end of the course the student:
- - knows the vocabulary related to her/his field of study;
- - analyzes academic oral/written texts on the language and text level;
- - can work with the English texts related with her/his field of study;
- - converse wbout what they have read and heard.

- After passing the course student
- * knows the peculiarities of writing an academic text;
- * knows how to use the Institute of Education's thesis writing and formatting guide and refers correctly and according to the reference system;
- * can write an academic text based on both Estonian and English base texts;
- * knows the principles of process-oriented text creation and applies them in writing groups;
- * prepares a proper presentation and delivers it based on the academic style.

- After passing the course student can:
explain discipline's theoretical approaches & historical developments
analyse environmental issues as socially& culturally constructed/contested
apply anthropological perspectives to contemporary environmental debates
- explain the main theoretical approaches and historical developments in environmental anthropology;

analyse environmental issues as socially and culturally constructed, as well as politically and economically contested;

critically engage with ethnographic case studies addressing climate change, pollution, conservation, and environmental degradation;

assess how different societies understand, value, and interact with their environments at local, regional, and global scales;

apply anthropological perspectives to contemporary environmental debates and policy discussions;

communicate anthropological insights effectively in written and oral form.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Kursuse edukas sooritamine eeldab järjepidevat tööd terve semestri jooksul ja seminarides osalemist. 
Samuti eeldab kursuse läbimine:
- vähemalt kolmes loengus, kahes seminaris ja kollokviumil osalemist;
- vähemalt kolme õpipäeviku esitamist (sh õpipäevik erialakonverentsi põhjal);
- kõigi ülesannete õigeaegset esitamist;
- Padleti postituse tegemist;
- lõpupostituse tegemist foorumisse.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: HVKU.04.032 | Nimi (ET): Ühiskonna kultuuriline mõtestamine enne ja nüüd | Nimi (EN): Conceptualising Society Through the Lens of Culture, Past and Present | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe, magistriõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Teaduskond: humanitaarteaduste ja kunstide valdkond | Õppejõud: Elo-Hanna Seljamaa | Toimumisajad: Teisipäev | Kirjeldus: Kursuse esimeses pooles tutvutakse eesti talupoja maailmakäsitusega modernismieelsel ajal ja moderniseerumise algusajal ning allikatega, mille põhjal saab neid teemasid käsitleda. Arutletakse selle üle, mil moel mõjutasid talurahva elu seadused, regulatsioonid, mõisnike käsud, luterlik õpetus, rahvakombed ja -uskumused ning lojaalsus suguvõsale. Kursuse teises pooles käsitletakse kultuuri, folkloori ja kultuuripärandi mõistete ning etnograafiliste meetodite toel eelkõige identiteediga seotud protsesse tänases Eestis, mida kujundavad ränne, suurenenud mitmesus ja ebavõrdsus ning info- ja kommunikatsioonitehnoloogiad. | Hindamise eeltingimused: Kursuse edukas sooritamine eeldab järjepidevat tööd terve semestri jooksul ja seminarides osalemist. 
Samuti eeldab kursuse läbimine:
- vähemalt kolmes loengus, kahes seminaris ja kollokviumil osalemist;
- vähemalt kolme õpipäeviku esitamist (sh õpipäevik erialakonverentsi põhjal);
- kõigi ülesannete õigeaegset esitamist;
- Padleti postituse tegemist;
- lõpupostituse tegemist foorumisse. | Hindamise meetod: Punktide panek toimub jooksvalt. Kokku on kursuse eest võimalik saada kuni 100 punkti: 92 -100 punkti annab A, 84 - 91 puntki B, 76 -83 punkti C, 68 - 75 punkti D ja 60 - 67 punkti E.

opitulemused_en:
- Students will:
- 1. acquire a general knowledge of main era in theatre history (the classical antiquity, the middle ages, renaissance, etc);
- 2. learn to understand and analyze main content of each era and relations between them;
- 3. be capable of replacing the processes of theatre history into context of general history and understands the relations between the fields;
- 4. comprehend historical events in chronological order, stage terminology, concepts, genres and styles in theatre history;
- 5. knows key playwrights and their works of each era.

- -knows the basic elements of leadership;
-can conceptualize groups and processes from a managerial perspective and see their role in it as a leader;
-is familiar with the qualities, skills, activities and procedures that support leadership.

- The student successfully attended the course
- 1)	knows to situate a text in its discursive context ;
- 2)	knows to pay attention to the vocabulary use and nomination particularities in text ;
- 3)	has a knowledge of formal particularities of different text types and knows to identify them ;
- 4)	knows to constitute a text corpus in attention to the research problem ;
- 5)	knows to identify, in accordance to the research problem, research units in a text and lead a consequent analysis on it

- Upon completing the course, the student:
- - gains an understanding of the work of the Estonian media literacy network and the typical components and writing stages of media literacy development projects.;
- - deepens knowledge of the principles behind designing media literacy interventions;
- - practices creating educational materials and intervention projects for specific target groups' digital, media, and information literacy development.
- - Practices teaching, leadership, collaboration, communication, and problem-solving skills;
- - Develops the ability to critically assess and reflect on the impact of their created media literacy interventions;

- After completing the course, participants 
- are able to read unfamiliar academic texts; 
- recognise rhetorical devises, recognise the general organizational patterns of texts; 
- recognise major thought relationships; 
- can define concepts; 
- are able to draw an outline for longer texts and draft/compose short ones; 
- are able to refer, paraphrase, and avoid plagiarism.

- After passing the course student
- - be familiar with contemporary trends in mathematics didactics and teaching methodologies;
- - be able to critically analyse academic literature;
- - engage in discussions about research questions related to mathematics teaching at various educational levels;
- - participate in academic discussions and present their work both orally and in written form.

- A student who has successfully completed the course:
- 1. has a basic knowledge of some of the major issues and controversies in 20th and 21st century political theory;
- 2. can identify normative positions in philosophical and journalistic texts;
- 3. can reconstruct arguments and assess their persuasiveness.
- 4. can see the links between the author's approach to the problem and the contemporary historical context;
- 5. can identify and reconstruct polemics against the positions of other authors;
- 6. can critically evaluate these controversies, including deciding which arguments are stronger.
- 7. can discuss selected problems of political theory, formulating and defending normative positions.

- After the course, the students are expected:
- 1) has an overview of the requirements for composing and assessing the research papers;
- 2) realizes his/her role as a supporting research paper supervisor;
- 3) is able to formulate the rough title and the summary of the research paper based on the actual problem;
- 4) is able to give constructive feedback to student's work during different stages of supervision.

- Upon successfully  passing the course students will be able to:
- - differentiate between political systems based on combinations of power structures in a given society;
- - critically assess the concept of political system and its usability as an analytical tool;
- - know and understand different political systems;
- - understand and use the comparative method;
- - critically assess the effects that differences in political systems have for international relations.

- On successful completion of the course the student:
- 1.	can explain the development and characteristics of economy in contemporary Japan;
- 2.	can analyse Japanese economy in broader Asian context;
- 3.	understands the background of EU-Japan economic and trade relations, knows main documents and developments;
- 4.	understands the Japanese business culture and is ready for communication with partners.

- Upon completion of the course, the student is able to:
- 1. define and correctly use the core concepts of comparative politics;
- 2. identify and explain the main problems, research topics, and the major theoretical and methodological approaches in comparative politics;
- 3. describe key differences among political systems and explain the causes and consequences of these differences;
- 4. describe and critically assess important recent trends in the development of political systems and societies;
- 5. apply the core concepts, theories and methods of comparative politics to analyze contemporary political phenomena, problems and developments.

- After the course, the student:
- will understand the importance and meaning of religion in the daily life of Muslims;
- can analyze the role of Islam in broader society and the life of individuals;
- is aware of and has an overview of the beliefs, customs, practices, and rules of conduct arising from the diversity of Islamic countries;
- understands the peculiarities between the sexes and the role of the family in an individual's life;
- can discuss religious and cultural key issues of the Islamic world;

- Student who has completed the course:
- * argues on the effects of pollutants, removal methods and minimization of use;
- * analyzes the distribution of the selected pollutant in the environment and expresses it in creative written work;
- * applies basic chemistry skills in computational tasks (concentrations, equilibrium, Henry's law, redox);
- * analyzes the chemical content of complex biodegradation parameters;
- * knows the stages of wastewater treatment and calculates the main values of wastewater load indicators;
- * assesses the environmental problems of waste management related to oil shale processing.

- Learner who has completed the course:
- 1) has in-depth knowledge of solving cases including the fields of private, public and criminal law;
- 2) solves complex cases in a methodically correct manner, presenting systematic, comprehensive and accurate solutions, using correct Estonian legal language;
- 3) use the relevant legal provisions, relevant case-law and literature in solving the complex cases;
- 4) presents reasoned, logical and coherent positions in the resolution of complex cases;
- 5) is familiar with the current legal problems in the three areas, is able to identify them when solving various cases and to analyse them in depth and critically.

- The student:
- - knows the basics of planning communication;
- - knows how to use main tools and understands specifics related;
- - is capable of planning communication plans on basic level.

hindamise_meetod:
Eksam koosneb kahest osast. Esimeses osas on 10 mitme võimaliku õige valikvastusega küsimust (kokku 10 punkti), mis  puudutavad rahvusvahelise õiguse põhimõisteid ja doktriini, ajalugu, kontseptsioonide vahelisi seoseid. 
Teises osas analüüsitakse igakülgselt ette antud õigusprobleemi ning pakutakse küsimusele rahvusvahelisest õigusest lähtuv lahendus. Spetsiifilisi kaasuse lahendamise tehnikaid ei nõuta.
Eksamid on kirjalikud ja klassiruumis.

Eksamil hinnatakse:
- vastuses peegelduvat teadmiste täpsust ning sügavust;
- oskust näha seoseid erinevate õigusprobleemide vahel;
- oskust seostada teooriat rahvusvaheliste suhete praktikaga;
- formuleeringute täpsust ja väljendusoskust.

kirjeldus:
Aine kood: OIAO.07.075 | Nimi (ET): Rahvusvaheline õigus | Nimi (EN): International Law | EAP: 6.0 | Semester: kevad | Õppeastmed: bakalaureuseõpe | Õppetöö vorm: päevaõpe | Keel: eesti keel | Hindamisskaala: Eristav (A, B, C, D, E, F, mi) | Linn: Tartu linn | Teaduskond: sotsiaalteaduste valdkond | Õppejõud: Alexander Lott, Katre Luhamaa, Lauri Mälksoo, Liina Lumiste, Merilin Kiviorg | Toimumisajad: Teisipäev | Kirjeldus: Õppeaines käsitletakse rahvusvahelise avaliku õiguse olemust, teoreetilisi aluseid, ajaloolist arengut, allikaid, subjekte ning rahvusvahelise ja siseriikliku õiguse suhet. Samuti käsitletakse rahvusvahelist vastutust, rahvusvahelisi organisatsioone, diplomaatilist ja konsulaarõigust ning vaidluste lahendamist. Praktikumide ja seminaride käigus analüüsitakse teemadega seonduvaid teoreetilisi küsimusi ja rahvusvahelist praktikat. | Eeldusained: (OIAO.06.068 "Õiguse süsteem ja meetod") VÕI (OIAO.06.049 "Õiguse entsüklopeedia") VÕI (P2OG.02.251 "Õiguse süsteem ja meetod") VÕI (P2OG.02.149 "Õiguse entsüklopeedia"); (P2OG.02.058 "Riigiõigus") VÕI (OIAO.05.040 "Riigiõigus") | Hindamise eeltingimused: Hinne kujuneb kirjaliku eksami tulemusel. 
Kirjalikule eksamile pääsemise eelduseks on kõigi nelja seminari edukas läbimine sh vajalike kohustuslike kirjalike tööde sooritamine. | Hindamise meetod: Eksam koosneb kahest osast. Esimeses osas on 10 mitme võimaliku õige valikvastusega küsimust (kokku 10 punkti), mis  puudutavad rahvusvahelise õiguse põhimõisteid ja doktriini, ajalugu, kontseptsioonide vahelisi seoseid. 
Teises osas analüüsitakse igakülgselt ette antud õigusprobleemi ning pakutakse küsimusele rahvusvahelisest õigusest lähtuv lahendus. Spetsiifilisi kaasuse lahendamise tehnikaid ei nõuta.
Eksamid on kirjalikud ja klassiruumis.

Eksamil hinnatakse:
- vastuses peegelduvat teadmiste täpsust ning sügavust;
- oskust näha seoseid erinevate õigusprobleemide vahel;
- oskust seostada teooriat rahvusvaheliste suhete praktikaga;
- formuleeringute täpsust ja väljendusoskust.

opitulemused_en:
- Students completing the Master's Exam:
- 1. have acquired essential knowledge and skills in IT;
- 2. are qualified to resolve legal matters in IT;
- 3. are qualified to work in a group effectively and in an organised manner.

- Upon the completion of the course the student:
- 1) understands the nature of the sociological perspective and is able to observe social processes at both macro and micro levels;
- 2) knows and is able to identify the links between the different parts of the individual and the structure of the society;
- 3) understands and analyses the nature of culture, intercultural differences and their impact on human behaviour at micro and macro levels;
- 4) applies sociological knowledge to address problems and challenges in society.

- The student:
- - knows the basic terminology related to the subject;
- - knows more frequent models or examples and case studies.

kirjeldus_et:
Kursus on mõeldud üliõpilastele, kes ei ole varem ukraina keelt õppinud. Kursuse raames antakse algteadmisi ukraina					keelest, mis võimaldaks suhelda lihtsamates vestlussituatsioonides, ning baasteadmisi grammatikast. 						Kursuse teemad: 
					- enesetutvustus;
					- pere ja sugulased;
					- ametid ja töökohad;
					- minu kodumaa ja -linn;
					- sisseostude tegemine ja reisimine;
					- arvsõnad, telefoninumbrid, aadress;
					- ilm;
					- vaba aeg ja hobid;
					- kellaaeg;
					- minu kodu.

Grammatika põhiteemad: 
					- nimisõnade ja omadussõnade käänamine;
					- isikulised ja omastavad asesõnad;
					- tegusõna oleviku, mineviku ja tuleviku vormid;

kirjeldus_en:
A course is meant for those who have never learnt Ukrainian before. It provides the basic knowledge and skills, likewise 					familiarizes the learners with the system of Ukrainian grammar. 
					The topics of the course: 
					- Introducing person;
					- Family and relatives;
					- Occupations;
					- My homeland and my home town;
					- Shopping and traveling 
					- Numerals, phone numbers and addresses;
					- Weather;
					- Leisure time and hobbies;
					- Time expressions;
					- My home.
The basic grammar:
					- declension of nominal categories;
					- personal and possessive pronouns;
					- verb forms in present, past and future tense.

opitulemused_en:
- After completing the course the student should be able to:
- - read and understand simple texts in Ukrainian;
- - use the vocabulary and grammar covered during the course in everyday situations;
- - get into social contact (to greet, to say goodbye, to introduce 	oneself, to thank, to apologize etc.);
- - talk about family, home town, hobbies, day schedule;
- - understand the basic structures of Ukrainian grammar;
- - ask simple questions and answer them.

kirjeldus:
