opitulemused_en:
- On successful completion of the course, the student:
- - will have a basic knowledge of the development of institutions, political systems and ideologies in the Estonian territory over the last 150 years in relation to international developments;
- - is able to analyse provided sources and relate them to historical and contemporary issues;
- - is able to participate in a discussion on central themes of Estonian political and intellectual history and is capable of formulating proper arguments;
- - is able to communicate the results of their research in a written form in a clearly argued and structured way, drawing on relevant sources.

- Successful student:
- * has the necessary knowledge, practical skills and experience to sing in a mixed choir;
- * has acquired basic knowledge of the basic theory of music;
- * knows composers, text authors, musical styles and aesthetics of music in the choir's repertoire;
- * has acquired basic knowledge of the basics of vocal technique, the sound unity of the vocal group and the sound image of a mixed choir;
- * has acquired the repertoire of the respective semester of the mixed choir.

- At the end of the course the student can:
- * understand short and simple texts related to their future professions;
- * use specialized medical terminology learned during the course and apply the acquired vocabulary to their working lives;
- * correctly use the terminology and grammar acquired during the course;
- * use the acquired terminology both in oral and written form.

- The student:
- - knows the main goals of sustainable development;
- - knows how to analyze links between sustainable development and culture management;
- - knows the main goals and practices of sustainable culture management.

- The student:
- - knows main type of projects and processes;
- - understands the role of cultural management in the sector;
- - knows main expectations to cultural management professionals.

- After passing the cours, the student:
- 1) has an overview of the rules and practices of scientific research;
- 2) knows the rules and methods of referencing;
- 3) knows different ways and and rules of research reporting and presentation;
- 4) knows the pecularities of the geological research and reporting.

