can create word frequency lists from text;
knows how to search co-occurrences of phenomena from text.

- Learning outcomes: after passing the course student:
- 1. Understands the principles of technical drawing and mechanical drafting and is able to apply ISO standards in practice;
- 2. Is able to analyse spatial objects, decompose them into simpler geometric elements, and plan an appropriate modelling strategy;
- 3. Is familiar with the basic workflows of SolidWorks and can use the software to create simple 3D models and related technical drawings;
- 4. Can prepare a manufacturing-oriented technical drawing of a part containing approximately 10–20 dimensions, selecting an appropriate number of views and sections and applying ISO-compliant dimensioning;
- 5. Solves modelling tasks independently and creatively, making justified technical decisions within given degrees of freedom;
- 6. Is able to use basic measuring tools (e.g. a vernier caliper) and apply fundamental 3D printing techniques for producing simple parts.

- After passing the course student
- KNOWLEDGE
explains the theoretical foundations of freedom of expression and their application in public communication;

describes the principles regulating public communication and the core elements of professional ethics;

analyses the control and oversight systems operating in society in relation to freedom of expression and communication practice.
- SKILLS
applies the relevant ethical and legal principles of the field when analysing conflicting communication cases;

assesses potential conflicts between freedom of expression and other rights or principles and justifies the decisions made;

selects an appropriate course of action in complex situations, based on the ethical and legal frameworks of public communication.
- GENERAL COMPETENCES
interprets texts of different functions and styles, taking into account their context and purpose;

uses sources accurately and in a methodologically justified manner, following academic referencing standards;

critically analyses and reflects on their own knowledge and learning experience, identifying further development and improvement needs.

