- Upon successful completing the subject, master students:
- - will acquire skills of systematic cooperation with their supervisor;
- - will draw up a research plan for a semester and be able to critically analyze its fulfillment;
- - will associate theoretical standpoints of their research topics with appropriate methods of analysis and the empirical material to be analyzed in their research work;
- - will implement necessary methods for an analysis of the empirical material in academic writing, proceeding from the topic of their research work ;
- - will acknowledge basic principles of academic writing and be able to apply them in compiling master's theses;
- - will be able to express in a well-reasoned manner fundamental positions of their research topic in an academic presentation.

- At the end of the course, students should:
- - have acquired an understanding of the major concepts in machine learning and around the use of deep neural networks in particular, and of the practical considerations related to building and using such models; in general terms as well as with domain specific considerations for molecular biology;
