- - analyses how conspiracy theories influence health, communication, technology, religion, science, and political processes;
- - evaluates arguments for and against conspiracy theories using critical thinking and evidence-based reasoning;
- - recognizes the psychological, social and cultural factors that contribute to conspiracy thinking and radicalization;
