Complete all assignments successfully (quizzes, individual homework, group work);
AND participate in at least 60% (6 out of 10) of lectures;
AND participate in the seminar where their group presents the results of the group work;
AND participate in the seminar dedicated to retrospective for the group work.

opitulemused_en:
- Course participants
- will be able to use the advanced language structures and vocabulary covered during the course;
- will be able to understand and orally summarize complex texts;
- will be able to apply the principles of making academic presentations.

- After passing the course student
- A student who has completed the course:
* uses grammatical cases and case inflections of the Estonian language in the singular, the nominative case also in the plural;
* turns verbs into the present and simple past tense;
* uses ma- and da-verbs;
* compares adjectives;
* uses ordinal numbers I-XII;
* introduces themselves;
* talks about their studies and day;
* describes their own and others' appearance and clothing;
* compares things, people and situations.

hindamise_eeltingimused:
Semestri lõpuks positiivse tulemuse (A, B, C, D, E) saamiseks peab kursusel osaleja:
1) osalema aktiivselt vähemalt 24 ainetunnis (80% kõigist tundidest);
2) sooritama 2 auditoorset testi;
3) sooritama 2 harjutustesti (eeltesti) Moodle'is;
4) esinema hästi 2 vestlustunnis teemadel "Mina, minu huvid ja õpingud" ning "Minu kiire päev Tartus".

kirjeldus_et:
Ainekursus õpetab igale inimesele vajalikke ning olulisi baasoskusi igapäevaseks eluks digitaalses maailmas. Kursuse jooksul käiakse ühiselt läbi kolm oskuste plokki: 

1.	kuidas kujundada ja hallata oma vajadustest lähtuvat digiprofiili ning esitleda ennast digikeskkonnas (professionaalne CV, digitaalse identiteedi kujundamine, sotsiaalmeedia kasutamine);

2. kust ja kuidas leida, koguda ning analüüsida infot digivahendite abil (veebiküsitlused, andmete kogumine ja tõlgendamine, statistika ja mõõdikud, digiarhiivid, tehisaru tööriistad);

3. kuidas tegutseda digitaalselt aktiivse ja teadliku kasutajana (osalemine ühiskondlikes protsessides, digiturvalisus ja andmekaitse, digitaalne õigusruum, digitaalse sisu loomine ja jagamine).

Kursus annab parema arusaamise digivõimalustest meie elus ning annab osalejatele tööriistakasti, mis on vajalik digitaalses maailmas paremaks orienteerumiseks ning informatsiooni otsimiseks, leidmiseks ning esitlemiseks. 

Kogu kursus on üles ehitatud praktilistele harjutustele. Enne igat praktilist harjutust antakse ülevaade digiühiskonna erinevatest arengutest, sh info teke ja esitlus, õigusloome, andmete usaldusväärsus, tehisintellekti kasutamine, inimese, kodaniku ja spetsialisti roll erinevates tegevustes jne.

kirjeldus_en:
The course teaches every person necessary and important skills for everyday life in the digital world. During the course, three skill blocks are jointly covered:

1. how to design and manage a digital profile based on personal needs and present oneself effectively in digital environments (professional CV, digital identity development, use of social media);

2. where and how to find, collect, and analyse information using digital tools (web-based surveys, data collection and interpretation, statistics and metrics, digital archives, AI tools);

3. how to act as a digitally active and informed participant (engagement in societal processes, digital security and data protection, understanding the digital legal environment, creating and sharing digital content).

The course gives a better understanding of various digital possibilities in our lives and gives the participants a toolbox, which is necessary for better orientation in the digital world and for searching, finding and presenting information.

The whole course is built on practical exercises. Before each practical exercise, an overview of the development of various aspects of the digital world is given, including the generation and presentation of information, legislation, data reliability, the use of artificial intelligence, and the role of the person, citizen and specialist in various digital activities.

opitulemused_en:
- Professional knowledge and skills. After successfully passing the course, the student can:
- - design and manage their digital identity, prepare a professional CV, and connect acquired digital competences with further academic and career development;
- - apply the principles of digital security, data protection, and the digital legal environment, and act safely and ethically in digital settings;
- - participate as a digitally active citizen in societal processes, using digital tools in an informed and responsible way;
- - design web-based surveys, collect and analyse data, and interpret statistics, metrics, and indicators;
- - use quantitative methods, digital archives, and datasets in research, and apply AI tools purposefully and critically;
- - plan, implement, and present their research topic in different formats, including visual and audiovisual forms;
- - use social media strategically to increase the visibility and impact of their work, ideas, and research results;
- - initiate and develop simple digital solutions or projects using creative, collaborative, and problem-solving approaches;
- - reflect on their learning experience, evaluate the development of their digital competences, and relate acquired knowledge and skills to academic, professional, and societal contexts.

