opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course student
- - able to see and evaluate individual bodily movement possibilities;
- has further developed coordination and body memory;
- can better control their body positions and movement quality;
- is able to assess his own physical fitness and avoid injuries/overload.

- After passing this course every student:
- 1) is able to define the Darboux sums and prove Riemann's condition for integrability;
- 2) is familiar with the notion of the Riemann integral;  is able to formulate and prove the fundamental theorem of calculus; knows the definitions of improper integrals, is able to test the onvergence of noncomplicated integrals;
- 3) is familiar with the notion of uniform convergence of sequences and series of functions; by means of the Weierstrass test, recognizes uniformly convergent series; is able to find the interval of convergence of a power series and to prove the main properties of the sum of it; knows the notions of Taylor series and Fourier' series.
- 4) chooses suitable mathematical conceptions for problems, and is able to apply these conceptions while solving problems;
- 5) investigates and compiles logic reasonings within the framework of course material;
- 6) has developed mathematical written self-expression skills in tests and mathematical oral self-expression skills in practicals, lectures and final exam.

- After completing the course students will be able to
- 1) conveys the main content of articles written on current topics in his/her own words;
- 2) analyzes the main content of different media sources;
- 3) participates in discussion on the topic studied; expresses his/her points of view and brings out arguments for and against different opinions;
- 4) talks in detail about a matter related to Estonia;
- 5) prepares a proper slide presentation.

- After having successfully completed the course, the student:
- * is capable of identifying and debating key philosophical issues related to the rapid development of artificial intelligence and its impact on the concept of mind;
- * has enhanced their philosophy-specific written and oral communication and argumentation skills.
- More specifically, the student:
- * has explored issues related to the transformation of the concept of mind, human identity, and agency in the age of AI;
- * has applied critical thinking to real-world challenges, anticipating future developments of AI and their broader impacts on humanity;
- * has formulated and defended some solutions to philosophical problems that need to be addressed in order to make progress on real-world challenges related to developments in AI technology;
- * has practiced discussing and assessing the ethical and societal implications of AI on future human cognition and society, fostering responsible perspectives.

- The students will know:
- 1) the recent major general breakthroughs in the field of synthetic biology;
- 2) major applications of synthetic biology in bio-economy;
- 3) major applications of synthetic biology in medicine;
- 4) major applications of synthetic biology in agriculture;
- 5) major applications of synthetic biology in chemical and material industry;
- 6) major applications of synthetic biology in the fields of biofuels, global warming, and in reaching the humanities goals of biosustainability.

- After successful completion of the course, the student
- - has an idea of the biological levels and complexity of behavior regulation
- - can describe modern biological psychology research fields and topics
- - have acquired the basic concepts of biological psychology;
- - has knowledge of the molecular, cellular and systemic basic mechanisms of an individual's internal regulation and behavior;
- - knows and can describe research methods used in the field;
- - understands the experimental designs and models used to study the biological bases of behavior;
- - is able to relate different subfields of biological psychology and ask relevant questions;
- - is aware of ethical issues in the field of research.

- A student of the University of Tartu who completed the course:
- a) understands the basics of communication-based language learning; formulates and explains the starting points of communication-based language learning;
- b) applies communication-based language learning techniques in practical learning activities in communication with a language friend;
- c) effectively plans communication-based language learning activities;
- d) develops language, cultural and social competences, cooperation and time management skills.
- A student of Narva College of the University of Tartu who completed the course:
- a) develops communication competence in Estonian;
- b) deepens his knowledge of the different communication methods and norms of the Estonian language, the Estonian communication and cultural space and society;
- c) understands the basics of communication-based language learning; formulates and explains the starting points of communication-based language learning;
- d) applies communication-based language learning techniques in practical learning activities in communication with a language friend;
- e) effectively plans communication-based language learning activities;
- f) develops language, cultural and social competences, cooperation and time management skills.

- student:
- * knows physiotherapeutic treatments for various traumas, orthopedic disorders and overload syndromes;
- * understands the relationship between physiotherapeutic assessment and therapy associated with a patient's musckoloskeletal dysfunction;
- * apply theoretical knowledge of the course in practice;
- * evaluates the quality of patient`s physiotherapy and his/her own development during the therapy process with the aim to provide high quality therapy to all patients during his/her future professional career.
- The subject course practice is related to the parts of career planning such as self-analysis (eg ability to analyze and interpret professional experience), knowledge of possibilities (eg have an idea of the professional identity of professions related to their specialty) and planning (eg ability to plan their working time).

- After passing this course the student:
- 1. is familiar with primitive roots, can find them and prove basic results about them;
- 2. is familiar with quadratic residues, Legendre and Jacobi symbols, can compute the values of those symbols and prove basic results about quadratic residues;
- 3. is familiar with simple applications of number theory in cryptography, including primality tests, Diffie-Hellman key exchange and the RSA cryptosystem.

hindamise_meetod:
Eksamisessiooni ajal toimub üks kontrolltöö. Lõpphinne kujuneb kontrolltöö põhjal järgmise hindamisskaala alusel:

vähemalt 90 punkti -- A;
80-89 punkti -- B;
70-79 punkti -- C;
60-69 punkti -- D;
50-59 punkti -- E;
vähem kui 50 punkti -- F.

Iga praktikumipunkt võib mõjutada lõpphinnet positiivses suunas 0.4 hindamisskaala punkti ulatuses (st 5 praktikumipunkti = 2 hindepunkti). Sellist mõju omavate punktide hulka ei arvestata kontrolltööle pääsemiseks vajalikku minimaalset punktisummat. 

NB! Mitterahuldavat hinnet praktikumipunktid rahuldavaks ei muuda.

