opitulemused_en:
- Student passing through the course:
* Knows and understands the main microscopy and physical analysis methods. Uses correctly (orally and in writing) the main terms of microscopy and physical analysis methods in both English and Estonian languages.
* Has base knowledge of the vacuum techniques used;
* Knows and understands the working principles of optical, scanning and transmission electron microscopes and scanning probe microscopes, electron and X-ray fluorescence- and electron spectrometers and X-ray microanalyzers, secondary ion mass-spectrometers, and knows their applications, where and for what this type of analyzing equipment are used;
* Obtains the first practical experiences for solid samples characterization with reflective optical-, scanning electron and atomic force microscopes, and X-ray fluorescence spectrometers, and with the preparation of the samples.

opitulemused_et:
- Kursuse lõpuks üliõpilane
- *	teeb vahet üld- ja oskuskeele vahel
- *	tabab kiiresti laia erialast teemaringi käsitlevate uudiste, artiklite, ülevaadete sisu ja asjakohasuse;
- *	oskab teha kokkuvõtteid keerukatest tekstidest; oskab neid resümeerida ja kommenteerida;
- *	oskab kirjalikus suhtluses selgelt ja täpselt väljenduda
- *	oskab õpitavate teemade piires kirjeldada, arutleda, arvamust avaldada, kommenteerida, sealjuures keeleteadmisi eesmärgipäraselt kasutades

opitulemused_en:
- Student who has completed the course
- *	knows the difference between standard language and language for special purposes;
- *	is able to quickly grasp the content and relevance of a wide range of news, articles, and overviews on specialized topics;
- *	is able to give a review of complex texts; is able to summarize and comment on these texts;
- *	is able to express him/herself clearly and concisely in written communication;
- *	is able to describe, discuss, give an opinion, and comment within the themes to be learned, while using linguistic knowledge for the purposes intended.

opitulemused_et:
- Õppeaine läbinud õppija:
- Üliõpilane: 
- mõistab indiviidi erinevaid rolle organisatsioonis;
- selgitab kommunikatsiooni mõiste tähendust, selle protsesse ja funktsioone, erinevaid mudeleid ning avaliku kommunikatsioone vorme;
- mõistab avaliku kommunikatsiooni rolli ja sotsiaalse turunduse tähendust ning nende kasutamise tähtsust noorsootöös;
- seostab erinevaid võimalike gruppide ja organisatsiooni omavahelisi seoseid;
- selgitab juhtimise ja kvaliteedijuhtimise mõiste olemust ja põhitegevust, sh asjaajamistoimingud;
- mõistab olulisimaid juhtimisteooriaid ja nende praktilisi rakendusvõimalusi;
- mõistab kaasaegsele juhile vajalikke kompetentse ja juhtimisfunktsioone, sh kommunikatsiooniprotsesside ja funktsioonide erinevaid mudeleid;
- analüüsib organisatsiooni, selle toimimise vastavust sise- ja väliskeskkonna teguritele.

opitulemused_en:
- After passing the course student
- The student: 
- understands different roles of an individual in an organization; to explain the meaning of the concept of communication, its processes and functions, different models and forms of public communication;
- understands the role of public communication and the importance of social marketing and the importance of using them in youth work; 
- establishes different relationships between potential groups and the organisation; 
- explains the nature and the core business of the concept of management and quality management, including business operations;
- understands the most important management theories and their practical applications;
- understands the competence and management functions required for a modern leader, including various models of communication processes and functions; 
- analyses the organization, its performance against internal and external factors.

